{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor","id":1057140,"title":"Reach to switch primary factor ...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-02T09:58:27-08:00","id":1057140,"title":"Reach to switch primary factor ...","content":"... is the worst rule in 2e.<br /> <br /> It's the new speed bump. It makes little sense in Creative Thaumaturgy that you can't just make the spell that you want with the Primary factor that you want. Many times there are multiple interpretations of what a more powerful version of a spell would be, so I don't find this to be valid argument either.<br /> <br /> I'm going to house rule it away, but one of the problems is that it affects Legacy Attainments, which is a lot of fiddling around to fix.<br /> <br /> What's the justification for this? It seems really silly, especially when you can change 5 words in a published spell, call it a different spell and get around the rule anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:44:14-08:00","id":1057150,"title":"","content":"Hey Johnny Awesome,<br /> <br /> I really have no problem with the current 2E Creative Thaumaturgy aside from Unveling and Knowing, those 2 Practices really stomp me a lot of times regarding what kind of spells fall into those two categories and the major difference. Anyone with some tips on that regard would definitely be appreciated!<br /> <br /> As for the justification? I think the primary factor for 99% of the spells were done well and have no problem with them. However, it does appear you have run into some you don't agree with, do you have some examples that seem to be conflicting? Also, it might be possible a spell could have gone either way and it was a decision based on theme/balance that weighed into the final product. Also like you mentioned, CT is there to create a new spell with the desired Primary Factor and thus go that route to see how things work out.<br /> <br /> Obviously for some spells, spending a reach to change the primary factor to duration does not even make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:55:54-08:00","id":1057156,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I decided to add on more to my thoughts regarding Reach to change Primary Factor. Probably to allow people to make changes to a Rote they learned from Bob the Mage, who felt Duration was the key for his spell, but for your uses it is much better for Potency since your goals and purposes do not align with his. Thus you can use one of those Free Reaches to adjust the spell to your desired effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:56:40-08:00","id":1057158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor#post1057140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... is the worst rule in 2e.<br /> <br /> It's the new speed bump. It makes little sense in Creative Thaumaturgy that you can't just make the spell that you want with the Primary factor that you want. Many times there are multiple interpretations of what a more powerful version of a spell would be, so I don't find this to be valid argument either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen. It's a bizarre rule. The best justification I can think of is to help new players figure out where to put their free factors. But, as you said, the Reach requirement flies in the face of the Creative Thaumaturgy system, which should absolutely allow a Mage to imagine up a factor flipped version of any spell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:32:37-08:00","id":1057190,"title":"","content":"I think (I could totally be wrong here) that it was said at some point that that rule is there to make mages Reach more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:52:22-08:00","id":1057200,"title":"","content":"A rule of thumb is:<br /> <br /> - Is effect feast-or-famine Potency reliant? Then go Potency as Primary, no exceptions<br /> <br /> - Is effect pretty much OK with Potency 1, and it's more iconic for it's magic to be more persistent? Duration<br /> <br /> With a bonus round of<br /> &quot;If your spells is Potency reliant, BUT it's primary concerns are Clash of Wills , Duration is your road&quot;<br /> <br /> It's little unintuitive at first, but Duration is much more than simply &quot;how long your spell lasts&quot; - it's also &quot;how deeply anchored it is to the Fallen World&quot;. Persistence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:04:50-08:00","id":1057206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057190#post1057190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think (I could totally be wrong here) that it was said at some point that that rule is there to make mages Reach more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that's not the case. It's a terribly artificial way to force players to interact with the system, especially given that subsequent books are almost certain to add yet further Reach options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:13:16-08:00","id":1057211,"title":"","content":"It was less &quot;force to Reach more&quot; and more &quot;avoid creating 1001 variants of the same spell in order to milk that one extra Reach for free&quot;. It also makes Combined Casting much trickier, which is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:22:46-08:00","id":1057216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057211#post1057211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was less &quot;force to Reach more&quot; and more &quot;avoid creating 1001 variants of the same spell in order to milk that one extra Reach for free&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't that exactly what the rules achieves? Creative Thaumaturgy absolutely allows you to invent factor swapped versions of spells, so every spell is essentially fractured into two spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057211#post1057211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also makes Combined Casting much trickier, which is good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it good though? Mage already has a lot of bits to keep track of, especially compared to the other gamelines. I know my players are non-plussed when the system hurls additional non-narrative barriers in between their intent and the effect.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mind you, none of this is to say that Mage's casting system is bad. It's amazingly elegant for how much it seeks to achieve. This particular bit just seems weirdly unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-02-2017, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:24:56-08:00","id":1057217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057150#post1057150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Johnny Awesome,<br /> <br /> I really have no problem with the current 2E Creative Thaumaturgy aside from Unveling and Knowing, those 2 Practices really stomp me a lot of times regarding what kind of spells fall into those two categories and the major difference. Anyone with some tips on that regard would definitely be appreciated!.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowledge grants information. Unveiling changes your ability to gain or process information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:32:30-08:00","id":1057223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057217#post1057217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Knowledge grants information. Unveiling changes your ability to gain or process information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you sir, that is a much better way of looking at it. I was thinking more like Knowing is a radar ping while Unveiling is taking a good look through some type of binoculars, but I suppose they both kind of mean the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:45:27-08:00","id":1057230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057216#post1057216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't that exactly what the rules achieves? Creative Thaumaturgy absolutely allows you to invent factor swapped versions of spells, so every spell is essentially fractured into two spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you can't, as per page 127, &quot;The Primary Factor of a given spell effect is always the same; you can\u2019t make a creative thau- maturgy spell that\u2019s identical to another spell except with a different Primary Factor.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's the rule I really think is nonsense. Being able to change a spell's Primary Factor with a Reach makes sense to me, in case you want to cast a Rote you know with a different Primary Factor than it normally uses. But to be unable to creatively cast a similar spell with a different Primary Factor is really silly to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057216#post1057216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Mind you, none of this is to say that Mage's casting system is bad. It's amazingly elegant for how much it seeks to achieve. This particular bit just seems weirdly unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:08:38-08:00","id":1057242,"title":"","content":"If you're running everything with Creative Thaumatury, it's not very useful.<br /> <br /> However every Praxis spell, Rote spell, and Legacy attainment that is a set spell with a set primary factor now has an option to let you adjust that primary factor at a cost.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the problem is exactly. For when you're not using Creative Thaumaturgy, it's a useful option to have. If you're using Creative Thaumaturgy, you can get around needing to use it, but then you're giving up on all the bonuses from all those other options.<br /> <br /> I'm also with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> on the idea that the primary spell factor should make sense for the spell you're making, not just be something you pick because it's better for your mechanically. It's not necessarily hard to come up with similar spells that would have flipped primary factors, but it should at least make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:11:05-08:00","id":1057243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057230#post1057230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you can't, as per page 127, &quot;The Primary Factor of a given spell effect is always the same; you can\u2019t make a creative thau- maturgy spell that\u2019s identical to another spell except with a different Primary Factor.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's the rule I really think is nonsense. Being able to change a spell's Primary Factor with a Reach makes sense to me, in case you want to cast a Rote you know with a different Primary Factor than it normally uses. But to be unable to creatively cast a similar spell with a different Primary Factor is really silly to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you serious!? What is the possible benefit of this? All this does is confuse new players and make casting more frustrating.<br /> <br /> I'm at a loss trying to figure out why picking your Primary Factor at the time of casting is something that must be restricted. It's clearly not game breaking, otherwise the Reach option wouldnt be there. It's hardly OP, as others have said there are only a handful of spells for which you'd even want to use the option. It's a weird outlier rule with no apparent benefit. Doubly agreed OP, hands down the worst rule in 2e. All of 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-02-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:14:32-08:00","id":1057247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057230#post1057230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you can't, as per page 127, &quot;The Primary Factor of a given spell effect is always the same; you can\u2019t make a creative thau- maturgy spell that\u2019s identical to another spell except with a different Primary Factor.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's the rule I really think is nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, &quot;The exact same as this spell in the book but with a different primary factor&quot; feels really metagamey to me.<br /> <br /> If I have a spell that puts out a fire and uses Potency because it's a lasting effect making Duration meaningless, how does it make sense to make the same thing but with Duration instead?<br /> <br /> Instead you'd make a second spell, which has a different spell effect, which temporarily suppresses fire instead of actually putting it out. This is a different spell, with different implications.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:38:05-08:00","id":1057258,"title":"","content":"If I had to come up with a fluff reason for &quot;hard locked&quot; Primary Factors, I would spin a tale about, hmm...magic taking path of least resistance to survive in Fallen World. Like, it's just natural for spells that need Potency to *properly exist* to default for Primary Potency. Maybe I'm just biased, but I feel that key to understanding why these things are hardlocked is &quot;grokking&quot; that Duration and Potency are two alternative ways of &quot;making your spell more real/alive&quot;. But I can see why it's non-transparent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:43:21-08:00","id":1057262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057247#post1057247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, &quot;The exact same as this spell in the book but with a different primary factor&quot; feels really metagamey to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* I don't care about metagaming. Heck, CofD 2e encourages meta-game thinking in players on a system level, and I think it's better game for doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-02-2017, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:50:20-08:00","id":1057268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057247#post1057247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I have a spell that puts out a fire and uses Potency because it's a lasting effect making Duration meaningless, how does it make sense to make the same thing but with Duration instead?<br /> <br /> Instead you'd make a second spell, which has a different spell effect, which temporarily suppresses fire instead of actually putting it out. This is a different spell, with different implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you are saying is that the rule is there to make it more difficult to do something you wouldn't want to do in the first place?<br /> <br /> Again I ask; why bother with the rule at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:57:53-08:00","id":1057273,"title":"","content":"I think this thread needs a sample spell to illustrate the issue. I've got just the spell: Present as Past.<br /> <br /> Present as Past allows the mage to witness incoming futures and react to them in real time. It expresses this in two ways: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It reduces the Doors you face in Social Maneuvering.</li> <li>It causes everyone in combat to have to declare their actions before yours, and allows you to select when to act with perfect knowledge of your foes intentions.</li> </ol><br /> The first application is reliant on Potency. The second clearly favors duration. Both are entirely valid uses of the spell. However, as Present as Past has Potency locked as it's primary factor the second option requires additional reach or duration penalties to make use of. It's hard to argue that one function of the spell is better then the other, both are amazing in their respective fields. Different characters might buy this spell on Rote for different reasons, a socialite would find the Door reduction highly attractive, while a fighty type would love the confidence provided by the predictive initiative. However, the fighter has to sink additional reach into every casting, while the socialite is free to use that Reach elsewhere.<br /> <br /> This, in my eyes, is nonsense. Nothing but a speed bump in casting and a needless frustration to the Mage's player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-02-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:10:06-08:00","id":1057280,"title":"","content":"Present as Past would make more sense with a Withstand score (Since it's cast on subjects not the Mage himself) then Potency would apply to both its effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:13:45-08:00","id":1057282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057280#post1057280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Present as Past would make more sense with a Withstand score (Since it's cast on subjects not the Mage himself) then Potency would apply to both its effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, it's a problematic spell for numerous reasons (just try parsing a combat when 40% of characters have to declare their actions, while another is free to sorta jump around the initiative track), but it illustrates the Potency/Duration divide nicely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:20:54-08:00","id":1057285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057280#post1057280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Present as Past would make more sense with a Withstand score (Since it's cast on subjects not the Mage himself) then Potency would apply to both its effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't even noticed that the spell repeatedly refers to subjects - I guess a Resolve Withstand would make sense. Or alternatively make the Mage the subject of the spell, so it looks at future events from their perspective or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:17:19-08:00","id":1057313,"title":"","content":"My assumption was spells in the book were recipes illustrating what can be done with the magic system. Meaning, in a meta-game sense, you can draw inspiration AND ideas from published spells, then tweak stuff as you see fit.<br /> <br /> From a purely OUT-OF-GAME context, the spells in the book help the ST and PCs by providing a litany of rotes/spells to drive mysteries forward. If you didn't have the spells in the book, and only had the rules to make them, STs would have an immensely more difficult job.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> For inexperienced players, the spells in the book work as a road map or direct applications of spells holding their hand to a desired end (Present as Past).<br /> <br /> The main difference being that a player does not gain the benefits of rote casting if they're improvising a published effect. The rote version of the spell would thus be far more desirable.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why improvising a published spell with a changed default Primary factor is frowned upon other than getting away with not spending a Reach to change it.<br /> <br /> If you cast every published spell as an improvised spell just to avoid spending 1 Reach to switch, then you're not casting the spell as a rote. If you're casting the spell as a rote, you start from the get-go with a set Primary, but you also get rote benefits.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I also don't completely understand the &quot;Primary factor is whatever factor you think of when you imagine a stronger version.&quot; It just seems like deciding Primary factor should be up to whatever the player decides they want at the time. A stronger Mind Control spell? Or a longer lasting Mind Control spell? A hotter/more forceful flamethrower, or a weaker but longer burning flamethrower? (Maybe damage is overkill and you just need the narrative effect of a flamethrower to keep the shadow demons at bay.)<br /> <br /> If it doesn't matter and only serves to make the player happy because they get their way, why not let them choose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:04:03-08:00","id":1057366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057262#post1057262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug* I don't care about metagaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that there's plenty of acceptable/good metagaming and some people get too hung up on it, there's also plenty of points where it's still not good for the game.<br /> <br /> Metagame + narrative + game synergy for a good play experience is a great thing that the CofD 2e hits out of the ball frequently. I still don't want players deciding things for their characters as if the character's have read the books.<br /> <br /> To me, deciding which primary spell factor you want first is too much like playing your character like they read the rules of the game, rather than using the rules of the game to shape a fun experience with your character.<br /> <br /> The primary spell factor should stem from what the point of the spell is. That's why I said it isn't hard to create a spell that as the other primary spell factor, because it's not hard to come up with a spell where the other is clearly intrinsic to the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057268#post1057268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you are saying is that the rule is there to make it more difficult to do something you wouldn't want to do in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but the hyperbolic taking things to 11 stuff is making it hard to hear an actually question. Can you try again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again I ask; why bother with the rule at all? </div> </div> </div>You've yet to address the importance of the rule for Praxis/Rote/Attainment situations even if you ignore it for Creative Thaumaturgy. It has value for those alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057273#post1057273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this thread needs a sample spell to illustrate the issue. I've got just the spell: Present as Past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we perhaps pick a better option of a spell that doesn't have other issues (or if there isn't one in your mind... maybe just acknowledge that it's this spell not the rule)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first application is reliant on Potency. The second clearly favors duration. </div> </div> </div>I think the phrasing here is pretty telling. One application is <b>reliant</b> on Potency. One application <b>favors</b> more Duration.<br /> <br /> Lots of spells benefit from both. That's why you can increase both for any spell. If a spell relies on one of the two though, it should pretty obviously be that one.<br /> <br /> Also, really, if you have the Reach, Present as Past is better as Potency primary with Advanced Duration for it automatically lasting the scene allowing you to have the combat advantage to win a fight and then use the Doors advantage to, say, Force Doors on your opponent after you've beaten them up.<br /> <br /> And if you're in a pure combat scene, Acceleration is largely a more useful spell since it provides a lot more bonuses to combat while having a major advantage with Initiative manipulation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the fighter has to sink additional reach into every casting, while the socialite is free to use that Reach elsewhere. </div> </div> </div>This is true all over the place in the game. Combat time focused characters are inherently more Reach intensive than non-combat time focused characters, because there's a Reach requirement simply to act in combat time with most magic. Whether you like this aspect of the game or not, it's built into the whole game: magic when you have time is easier, and thus concepts that focus on pursuits that operate with lots of time have an easier time with being boosted with magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing but a speed bump in casting and a needless frustration to the Mage's player. </div> </div> </div>So, isn't the Reach to instant cast just as bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:52:41-08:00","id":1057386,"title":"","content":"I think the game will inherently endure some meta-gaming since characters will enjoy the benefits of taking actions that they may not be able to contextualize within the experience of their character. An example of this is when a character does something, or knows about something, that the player didn't know the character knew about. Not until successes are tallied does the basis of this knowledge materialize.<br /> <br /> The issue here is whether or not it can be explained within the context of the characters and the natural progress of their knowledge about things.<br /> <br /> If you're coming up with improvised spells that are only slight tweaks of published spells, you could reason that these spells are nothing but the natural evolution of playing around with the arcane practices. The fact that you <i>do not</i> cast a spell exactly as it is written would show that your character is not using the version of the spell that was codified by a master. You are naturally progressing through practices and arcana you can play with at your level. It isn't as though you have 1000 practices to delve through.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Yes, typically when people use Death Knowing spells they tend to bell-curve around a very common set of factors.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do people use rotes, then?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Because they're awesome, even if they require a bit of effort to wrangle into doing something removed from the primary intent of the rote when initially crafted.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why aren't there hundreds of different versions of 'Spell X' rotes?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Who says there aren't? Anyway, primarily because creating rotes is not a willy-nilly act and because 'approximate' copies already exist; however, if you're so inclined, you can make your own improvised version of 'Spell X' into a rote.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> It would be like playing the piano and happening across scales and chords by happenstance, which happens all the time. You just don't know what their official names are, or that they might be coded and sought after with particular zeal.<br /> <br /> The problem with denying the casting of spells that are too similar to rotes is that you've immediately defined a set of spells the mage cannot mold to his liking for some meta reason. Have they been platonically reinforced by the Supernal Realms? If this is the reason it make more sense, but it does certainly fly in the face of everything mage is setup to do.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 03-02-2017, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:15:36-08:00","id":1057399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057366#post1057366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that there's plenty of acceptable/good metagaming and some people get too hung up on it, there's also plenty of points where it's still not good for the game.<br /> <br /> Metagame + narrative + game synergy for a good play experience is a great thing that the CofD 2e hits out of the ball frequently. I still don't want players deciding things for their characters as if the character's have read the books.<br /> <br /> To me, deciding which primary spell factor you want first is too much like playing your character like they read the rules of the game, rather than using the rules of the game to shape a fun experience with your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is a point we're going to have to agree to disagree on, because I see no problem at all with players playing like the've read the book. Sure, their characters might not know the information in the book <i>as such</i>, but the information in the book serves to equip the players with knowledge that their characters, as inhabitants of the game world, could reasonably have. I'm of course okay with players electing to play characters who are inexperienced and do not possess all of that knowledge, but that's their choice, not something I would impose on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:05:31-08:00","id":1057437,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I'm gonna have to echo Charlaquin on the agree disagree thing. Bottom line is that I cannot imagine a scenario in which the Reach to Switch rule improves the enjoyment of anyone at the table. That, IMO, is the defining characteristic of a bad rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057262#post1057262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug* I don't care about metagaming. Heck, CofD 2e encourages meta-game thinking in players on a system level, and I think it's better game for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Metagaming is only bad when used abusively to break the plot. Metagaming in favor of the story improves the experience for all involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-03-2017, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T07:15:06-08:00","id":1057583,"title":"","content":"This is purely speculation on my part, but here it goes: Certain Spells, like &quot;Knit&quot; or &quot;World Walker&quot; don't have a Duration as such. They end immediately after taking effect, but when cast with a Duration they repeat themselves after each Ritual Casting interval. This essentially produces several castings for the price of one, so giving it an additional cost could be fair. Does anyone feel &quot;Reach to switch&quot; was designed with these effects in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:12:25-08:00","id":1057733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057437#post1057437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;617&quot;]Bottom line is that I cannot imagine a scenario in which the Reach to Switch rule improves the enjoyment of anyone at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't want to have to buy a bunch of Rotes twice so I can have them for each primary factor.&quot;<br /> &quot;I want to be able to use a Legacy Attainment in a slightly different fashion.&quot;<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, nobody's had fun not having to spend extra XP on stuff just for a minor mechanical advantage when the game lets them get that advantage for a temporary cost instead.<br /> <br /> I'm get that invoking the dreaded &quot;metagame&quot; was pointless, but that doesn't actually mean nothing else has been brought up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:49:35-08:00","id":1057751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057733#post1057733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;I don't want to have to buy a bunch of Rotes twice so I can have them for each primary factor.&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;I want to be able to use a Legacy Attainment in a slightly different fashion.&amp;quot;<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, nobody's had fun not having to spend extra XP on stuff just for a minor mechanical advantage when the game lets them get that advantage for a temporary cost instead.<br /> <br /> I'm get that invoking the dreaded &amp;quot;metagame&amp;quot; was pointless, but that doesn't actually mean nothing else has been brought up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like these problems are solved by keeping &quot;change Primary Factor&quot; as a +1 Reach option, without also requiring players to spend Reach to changing the Primary Factor of improvised spells that their characters theoretically made up themselves if what they want isn't &quot;what you immediately think of as a more powerful version of the spell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:52:27-08:00","id":1057753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057733#post1057733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't want to have to buy a bunch of Rotes twice so I can have them for each primary factor.&quot;<br /> &quot;I want to be able to use a Legacy Attainment in a slightly different fashion.&quot;<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, nobody's had fun not having to spend extra XP on stuff just for a minor mechanical advantage when the game lets them get that advantage for a temporary cost instead.<br /> <br /> I'm get that invoking the dreaded &quot;metagame&quot; was pointless, but that doesn't actually mean nothing else has been brought up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both those examples sound profoundly unfun yes. That's why I'd advocate &quot;choose your primary factor at the time of casting&quot;. No need to double buy rotes, no need to headache over attainments.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd like to point out that most of this conversation is founded purely in familiarity bias. If the Reach to Swap rule weren't in core, and someone came in proposing it be added, I'd venture everyone would be jumping down their throat over how pointless and speed bumpy such a rule would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-03-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:05:36-08:00","id":1057775,"title":"","content":"I guess ditching the &quot;primary factor&quot; line in spells and replacing it with &quot;Lasting: Yes/No/Possibly&quot; would be much better use of that line, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T18:51:45-08:00","id":1057869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057751#post1057751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like these problems are solved by keeping &quot;change Primary Factor&quot; as a +1 Reach option, without also requiring players to spend Reach to changing the Primary Factor of improvised spells that their characters theoretically made up themselves if what they want isn't &quot;what you immediately think of as a more powerful version of the spell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're in the realms of Creative Thaumaturgy, I still don't buy the argument that this is such an burdensome rule. If you can come up with a similar spell (see my fire extinguisher example), the rules don't force you to spend a Reach to have a different primary spell factor. The rules only say that you can't just create a spell that's otherwise identical but for the swapped primary factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057753#post1057753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both those examples sound profoundly unfun yes. That's why I'd advocate &quot;choose your primary factor at the time of casting&quot;. No need to double buy rotes, no need to headache over attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty big shift in stance to me. This is no longer, &quot;Reach to switch primary factor is a horrible rule,&quot; but that Primary factor as a set thing is a bad rule, which is a fairly different discussion in my mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to point out that most of this conversation is founded purely in familiarity bias. </div> </div> </div>This sounds a lot like, &quot;I don't actually have to make a case, because if you disagree with me and have read the book, you're automatically wrong, so I must be right!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Reach to Swap rule weren't in core, and someone came in proposing it be added, I'd venture everyone would be jumping down their throat over how pointless and speed bumpy such a rule would be. </div> </div> </div>Only if there's a significant other change (such as your above advocacy for no set primary factor). If the rules were otherwise completely identical we'd all want something because of the Praxis/Rote/Legacy Attainment issue.<br /> <br /> As well, I think there's a somewhat hypocritical nature to this as you've consistently made it sound like having to use Reach is horribly unfun, while spending Reach is the main way for Paradox to come into the game, and we're supposed to be all on board with the 2e conceit of engaging with Conditions/Breaking Points/Paradox/etc. as players because having our characters suffer negative stuff is fun.<br /> <br /> Even if people were complaining about it, wouldn't the obvious response be, &quot;but it makes it easier for things like Paradox to come into play by having Reach come up more!&quot; the same way things that bring on more Conditions to resolve are good? Because a lot of what you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> are saying are what I hear from people saying that adding Conditions in 2e was the flat out worst thing 2e has ever done (it's artificially forcing people to engage with the system for example is something I've seen from a lot of people that hate how much 2e spends on Conditions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:09:32-08:00","id":1057874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057869#post1057869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're in the realms of Creative Thaumaturgy, I still don't buy the argument that this is such an burdensome rule. If you can come up with a similar spell (see my fire extinguisher example), the rules don't force you to spend a Reach to have a different primary spell factor. The rules only say that you can't just create a spell that's otherwise identical but for the swapped primary factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I find the fact that you can't create an otherwise identical spell with swapped Primary Factors awkward and forced. If I'm creating the spell, why can't I create it with any Primary Factor I want? I get it with Rotes, and maybe Praxies, but if I'm making the spell, why isn't the Primary Factor up to me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057869#post1057869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, I think there's a somewhat hypocritical nature to this as you've consistently made it sound like having to use Reach is horribly unfun, while spending Reach is the main way for Paradox to come into the game, and we're supposed to be all on board with the 2e conceit of engaging with Conditions/Breaking Points/Paradox/etc. as players because having our characters suffer negative stuff is fun.<br /> <br /> Even if people were complaining about it, wouldn't the obvious response be, &quot;but it makes it easier for things like Paradox to come into play by having Reach come up more!&quot; the same way things that bring on more Conditions to resolve are good? Because a lot of what you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> are saying are what I hear from people saying that adding Conditions in 2e was the flat out worst thing 2e has ever done (it's artificially forcing people to engage with the system for example is something I've seen from a lot of people that hate how much 2e spends on Conditions).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for Pendragon, but Reach being unfun to spend is not the issue I take with the fixed nature of Primary Factors. I've got no problem with spending Reach. I take issue with the artificial limiting of creative thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T20:10:35-08:00","id":1057906,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, other than because you're okay with it (because many in this thread are not okay with it), why can't a mage utilize a spell with swapped primary factor?<br /> <br /> Everything about the rules says yes, but in-game the mage hits a hiccup and for some reason cannot do this one thing. This inability to do such a simple task seems like it should at the very least by thematically tied to the rules of the world.<br /> <br /> The best in-game reason I can think of is published spells are actually a list of some of the most frequently occurring spells in mage society/history (since time immemorial.)<br /> <br /> Or maybe they're imbued with higher meaning because of some grand war or important series of events. Perhaps the topic of an epic mystery. As such, whenever you go to cast a spell that is too close to a published spell, your primary factor utilizes the path of least resistance or its most comfortable pre-established orientation. Ergo, you don't always get the primary factor you want and must spend a Reach.<br /> <br /> If I do this, then I think I can work with the rules.<br /> <br /> But I completely understand why people would want to modify this rule to keep everything coherent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Interestingly, if a mage was inclined to probe they could see if any of their improvised spells have acquired this pattern of great importance. Basically, meta-gaming to see what is a published spell or rote. Perhaps it leads to the quest to find your soulmate or Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 03-03-2017, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T21:36:32-08:00","id":1057928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057874#post1057874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I find the fact that you can't create an otherwise identical spell with swapped Primary Factors awkward and forced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because primary spell factor is supposed to stem from the nature of the spell. Primary spell factor is literally the last thing you pick before casting a spell in creative thaumaturgy, and it is supposed to be an extension of the previous steps in the process. If you did the same thing in the previous four steps, you should end up with the same result in step 5. Doing something different in the previous steps (esp. the first one) means you're no longer making an identical spell.<br /> <br /> To me, wanting to do everything identical but the last step of the process is like saying you want to fire a gun without Firearms, but don't want to justify it by doing something different than just firing a gun normally. You don't get to swap Intelligence + Science (Ballistics) for Dexterity + Firearms to shoot someone in combat just because you want to &quot;science&quot; shoot them instead of normal shoot them. I can imagine situations where you can justify it (like having set up a remote firing gun-trap), but those situations are when you're doing something &quot;similar&quot; instead of &quot;identical.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Artificial&quot; is a useless term when we're talking about how to model something in an abstract game system, since it's all artificial. The magic system isn't modelling something real where we can point to limitations in the system being artificial constraints compared to how it actually works.<br /> <br /> You can't pick your primary spell factor directly, because you don't pick it directly. You pick it indirectly when you design the rest of the spell. Your character's ability to &quot;pick&quot; comes in when modifying spell factors as they actually cast the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057906#post1057906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms, other than because you're okay with it (because many in this thread are not okay with it), why can't a mage utilize a spell with swapped primary factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can? It just comes with a cost for the effort of switching.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything about the rules says yes, but in-game the mage hits a hiccup and for some reason cannot do this one thing. This inability to do such a simple task seems like it should at the very least by thematically tied to the rules of the world. </div> </div> </div>I'm really not sure what you mean here. The rules say you can flip them with Reach. What the rules say you can't do is design an identical spell but this one thing is flipped in the new spell. I think I've explained pretty thoroughly above on what I think that's the case, and how it doesn't constitute a &quot;hiccup&quot; of something they can do. Mages know to some extent that this is how magic works more easily, and if they want to push their magic in a different direction they either have to &quot;brute force&quot; it, or get creative with similar spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I completely understand why people would want to modify this rule to keep everything coherent. </div> </div> </div>I don't see any solid argument for it being incoherent. More people are arguing that they just don't want to deal with the restriction on grounds of fun, not coherence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:15:25-08:00","id":1057937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057928#post1057928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because primary spell factor is supposed to stem from the nature of the spell. Primary spell factor is literally the last thing you pick before casting a spell in creative thaumaturgy, and it is supposed to be an extension of the previous steps in the process. If you did the same thing in the previous four steps, you should end up with the same result in step 5. Doing something different in the previous steps (esp. the first one) means you're no longer making an identical spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what it sounds like to me. Step five of creative thaumaturgy says, &quot;Determine which Factor is the Primary Factor. This is either Potency or Duration, with the rule of thumb of \u201cwhichever Factor you immediately think of when you think of a more powerful version of the spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Great! So, when I think of a more powerful version of Present as Past, I think of a version that lasts longer, allowing me more combat rounds where I get to jump around the Initiative order as much as I want. But wait! The books says the primary factor is Potency... Weird, but ok, if I'm the one creatimg the spell, what I immediately think of is what matters, right? Oh, hang on. The paragraph continues. It says, &quot;The Primary Factor of a given spell effect is always the same; you can\u2019t make a creative thaumaturgy spell that\u2019s identical to another spell except with a different Primary Factor.&quot; So what gives? If the determining factor of Promary Factor is &quot;what you think of as a more powerful version of the spell&quot;, then why, when I can think of a more powerful version of one of the example spells, do I have to spend Reach to do it if whoever wrote the spell thought of something else as a more powerful version of it? Isn't this creative thaumaturgy? Aren't I the one creating the spell? And if so, shouldn't context matter when considering what is a more powerful version of the spell I want to create for a given situation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057928#post1057928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, wanting to do everything identical but the last step of the process is like saying you want to fire a gun without Firearms, but don't want to justify it by doing something different than just firing a gun normally. You don't get to swap Intelligence + Science (Ballistics) for Dexterity + Firearms to shoot someone in combat just because you want to &quot;science&quot; shoot them instead of normal shoot them. I can imagine situations where you can justify it (like having set up a remote firing gun-trap), but those situations are when you're doing something &quot;similar&quot; instead of &quot;identical.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the connection. What skill you use to fire a gun isn't a variable you select as part of the process of resolving firing a gun. What Factor is Primary is a variable you select as part of the process of creating a spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057928#post1057928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Artificial&quot; is a useless term when we're talking about how to model something in an abstract game system, since it's all artificial. The magic system isn't modelling something real where we can point to limitations in the system being artificial constraints compared to how it actually works.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't model anything in the real world, but the mechanics of creative thaumaturgy do model something in the narrative. Namely, the Mage forming an Imago on the fly, as opposed to using an internalized Imago (a Praxis), or memorized Imago (a Rote). And if part of that process is determining what constitutes &quot;a stronger version of that effect&quot;, it feels artificial to me that the Mage formulating the Imago doesn't determine what a stronger version of the spell they are inventing looks like. Why not? It's their spell. They made it up. And if making the Primary Factor Duration is something they feel is worth spending Reach on, evidently that's what a more powerful version of the spell looks like in this situation. Since the spell was crafted on the fly, for this particular situation, it's not very versimilar for that not to be the invented spell's Primary Factor to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057928#post1057928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't pick your primary spell factor directly, because you don't pick it directly. You pick it indirectly when you design the rest of the spell. Your character's ability to &quot;pick&quot; comes in when modifying spell factors as they actually cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can't always make that determination in a vacuum. If you could, there would never be a need to change a spell's Primary Factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-04-2017, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:45:07-08:00","id":1057940,"title":"","content":"I feel that &quot;Primary Factor is not a choice, it's a logical path of least resistance for the spell in question to take and making it go against it requires extra deliberate effort from the Mage represented by Reach&quot; would be much easier to swallow for a lot of people if the game actually went out to teach you about the concept and presented some sort of guideline that would help you absorb the logic and grok how to sort the &quot;this is obviously a Potency Primary kind of EFFECT, and this is obviously a Duration Primary kind of EFFECT&quot;. Notice I'm saying &quot;effects&quot;, not &quot;spells&quot;, to make sure you can do what you are saying - while it's probably obvious to you what exactly is the difference between Fireball Potency Primary and Fireball Duration Primary and how to make them different spells (good thing for the game) instead of palette-swapped convinience-fueled &quot;I just want more Duration&quot; identical spells (less good thing for the game, but not a bad thing for the game), I guess for a lot of people there simply isn't a good visible reason for that. I feel that's because you would need to go and reverse engineer majority of the spell list to find out the &quot;Primary Factor Sorting Logic&quot;, which isn't terryfingly fun for people who would rather just get the rule presented to them in the book so they can keep tinkering with the rules to minimum and focus on just *using* them. A lot of people would rather keep on researching in-game Mysteries in character instead of game-system Mysteries out of character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> So I guess that if you want to move the discussion forward and get a decent shot at convincing people about this issue here, I think a good way of doing it would be to unravel the inner workings of the system in a readable way and presenting the Primary Factor Sorting Logic in a form of a &quot;rulebook rule&quot;, giving enough examples (because a complete list would be...hard and counterproductive) with commentary on why this is such and such effect, so people can just learn from it and embrace the pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:47:53-08:00","id":1057941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057937#post1057937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great! So, when I think of a more powerful version of Present as Past, I think of a version that lasts longer, allowing me more combat rounds where I get to jump around the Initiative order as much as I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're confusing &quot;more powerful&quot; with &quot;better for how I want to use it.&quot; You're looking at it specifically as an extra flourish.<br /> <br /> The Primary Factor scales with your mastery of the spell's highest Arcanum. The primary factor is there to allow the spell to <i>do what it's supposed to do</i> \u2014 it's why so many Withstood spells are Potency-primary even if their effects are things you'd want to last a while, it's why most spells that &quot;make&quot; things or apply a persistent effect are Duration-primary even if their effects still scale with Potency, and it's why the primary factor <i>is the last thing to degrade from Dissonance</i>.<br /> <br /> Present As Past gives you a glimpse into the future. The socialite benefits more from it because the spell is sifting probabilities to <i>look into the immediate future</i>, and every other temporal perception spell in the book is Potency-based (to say nothing of the implicit Withstand the spell's reference to subjects brings to the table) \u2014 sensory Time magic operates on a default logic of taking glimpses, not gluing your eyes to the timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:01:21-08:00","id":1057943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057940#post1057940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that &amp;quot;Primary Factor is not a choice, it's a logical path of least resistance for the spell in question to take and making it go against it requires extra deliberate effort from the Mage represented by Reach&amp;quot; would be much easier to swallow for a lot of people if the game actually went out to teach you about the concept and presented some sort of guideline that would help you absorb the logic and grok how to sort the &amp;quot;this is obviously a Potency Primary kind of EFFECT, and this is obviously a Duration Primary kind of EFFECT&amp;quot;. Notice I'm saying &amp;quot;effects&amp;quot;, not &amp;quot;spells&amp;quot;, to make sure you can do what you are saying - while it's probably obvious to you what exactly is the difference between Fireball Potency Primary and Fireball Duration Primary and how to make them different spells (good thing for the game) instead of palette-swapped convinience-fueled &amp;quot;I just want more Duration&amp;quot; identical spells (less good thing for the game, but not a bad thing for the game), I guess for a lot of people there simply isn't a good visible reason for that. I feel that's because you would need to go and reverse engineer majority of the spell list to find out the &amp;quot;Primary Factor Sorting Logic&amp;quot;, which isn't terryfingly fun for people who would rather just get the rule presented to them in the book so they can keep tinkering with the rules to minimum and focus on just *using* them. A lot of people would rather keep on researching in-game Mysteries in character instead of game-system Mysteries out of character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> So I guess that if you want to move the discussion forward and get a decent shot at convincing people about this issue here, I think a good way of doing it would be to unravel the inner workings of the system in a readable way and presenting the Primary Factor Sorting Logic in a form of a &amp;quot;rulebook rule&amp;quot;, giving enough examples (because a complete list would be...hard and counterproductive) with commentary on why this is such and such effect, so people can just learn from it and embrace the pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiissssssss!!!!!!! If the rule for determining Primary Factor was based on more specific, objective criteria, it wouldn't be so verisimilitude breaking that the Primary Factor for a given effect is set in stone. If the Primary Factor of an effect is meant to be an objective quality, the criteria for determining it in creative thaumaturgy should not be subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:04:35-08:00","id":1057945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057941#post1057941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're confusing &quot;more powerful&quot; with &quot;better for how I want to use it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>By what metric do you evaluate the power of a creatively constructed spell if not its efficacy at executing the function its creator intended to use it for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-04-2017, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:20:02-08:00","id":1057949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057945#post1057945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By what metric do you evaluate the power of a creatively constructed spell if not its efficacy at executing the function its creator intended to use it for?</div> </div> </div> </div>By what metric do you judge wholesale duplication of a spell that's made for one thing with a toggle flipped to be &quot;creative construction&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:27:54-08:00","id":1057952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057949#post1057949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By what metric do you judge wholesale duplication of a spell that's made for one thing with a toggle flipped to be &quot;creative construction&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's made with creative thaumaturgy. By the book's own description, a spell is either a Rote, a Praxis, or improvised. If my character is improvising a spell, should she not be the one who determines what the spell she improvised is &quot;supposed to do&quot;?<br /> <br /> Out-of-character I may be picking something that's close enough to the effect I want from the list of example spells and making minor tweaks to it to suit my needs, because that is easier for me to do then to invent a brand new effect from whole cloth. In character, however, Lupa is improvising an Imago specifically for this situation. So why does she have to Reach a bit closer to (or beyond) her grasp to make the spell that she created on the fly scale the way she wants it to for the purpose she created it for? If she's not the arbiter of what her spell is &quot;supposed to do&quot;, then who or what is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-04-2017, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:32:12-08:00","id":1057953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057943#post1057943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiissssssss!!!!!!! If the rule for determining Primary Factor was based on more specific, objective criteria, it wouldn't be so verisimilitude breaking that the Primary Factor for a given effect is set in stone. If the Primary Factor of an effect is meant to be an objective quality, the criteria for determining it in creative thaumaturgy should not be subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kinda is, but it's &quot;hidden&quot; so unless you dig deeply into the inner workings of spells having the whole game in mind, you won't &quot;see it&quot; and won't have enough &quot;system context&quot; to see it as something other than &quot;it's an arbitary choice&quot;. Kind of like in DND 5e (I think you play it, but I might be remembering it wrong) it at first glance it may look weird that Cantrips don't do +Attribute to damage or, even more specifically, why Firebolt does 1d10 base damage while other cantrips do smaller dice, but after you play it enough (or read enough of it rules and recognize the patterns), it seems obvious. Fire does the most damage because there is unspoken (but emergant from the rest of the game, so we can assume it was a design choice and in DND 5e DESIGNER BIBLE, there is a line saying exactly this) rule that fire is supposed to be the most damaging element with fewest control and status effect riders, balanced by the fact that it's also the most resisted (well, second well after poison) element in the game...<br /> ...which you actually don't need to know in order to play OR game master the game. You don't need to dig so deeply into the inner workings of the system unless you want to homebrew for it. <br /> However, certain problems with Mage come from the fact that in order to &quot;just&quot; play or, even scarier, &quot;just&quot; GM the game you need to dig so deeply into it in order to use certain features (on player front, mostly Creative Thaumaturgy, but on GM front, *pretty much everything*) that you basically need to understand the system to the point of being able to &quot;homebrew it&quot; in informed way. <br /> Basically, you need to get to the unexposed bits of the system that are hidden behind the curtain. This is why there are endless arguments about &quot;Lasting or not??&quot;, by the way - game kinda assumes it's obvious what spells are Lasting or not, so it doesn't teach you about that. <br /> This is, in general, one of biggest beefs my group has with this game in general - I'm the only person interested in inner workings of systems and games to the point where I find it actively pleasant to disassemble and dissect games to understand them. They aren't. They don't feel a need to understand it and don't want to do the research; if they need to know something, they want the game to tell it to them. Our GM dislikes homebrewing (not the idea of it, but she doesn't like doing it) and one of her most common complaints about the system is that in a lot of places, it basically tells her &quot;I don't know, figure it out, you are the GM not me&quot; in places where she doesn't feel like making a judgement call because she feels like game doesn't provide her with enough information or examples to learn a pattern from. You can't even possibly imagine how much pain *writing up Mage NPCs* caused her because she literally had to study the game like it was midterms in order to even have a briefest idea of &quot;how could a Mage at my desired level of competency look like mechanically&quot;.<br /> In general, while running a game it's apparently pleasant enough to keep doing it, *prepping for it* is recurringly compared to unfun midterms cramming...to which you didn't take any notes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:38:57-08:00","id":1057955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057952#post1057952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my character is improvising a spell, should she not be the one who determines what the spell she improvised is &quot;supposed to do&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your character is improvising a spell to grant her an abiding view of the immediate future that is distinct from Present As Past, either she is not duplicating Present As Past with the primary factor flipped or she is going to have to contend with the same difficulties of forming an Imago that that spell imposes for that effect.<br /> <br /> It's one Reach. The specific spell under discussion in particular is available at a level of Arcanum mastery whose attendant Greater Utility Attainment frees up that same amount of Reach from instant casting. The specific spell under discussion is also not exempt from the normal mechanics allowing the expenditure of Reach for Advanced Duration and references subjects, which rather cuts down on the use of being able to readily make the effect last for multiple weeks. The specific spell under discussion \u2014 and <i>virtually every potential spell this discussion could conceivably apply to</i>, in fact \u2014 is not exempt from the many <i>many</i> ways around the problems that excess Reach presents for a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T01:01:18-08:00","id":1057965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057937#post1057937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what it sounds like to me. Step five of creative thaumaturgy says, &quot;Determine which Factor is the Primary Factor. This is either Potency or Duration, with the rule of thumb of \u201cwhichever Factor you immediately think of when you think of a more powerful version of the spell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing the disconnect. You can't figure out what you think of a more powerful version of the spell would be if you haven't done the first four steps, and if you do the first four steps the exact same way, the fifth step wouldn't have a reason to produce a different result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, when I think of a more powerful version of Present as Past... </div> </div> </div>Again, can we pick a different example? Present as Past is a distinctly problematic spell on a number of levels that makes it a poor choice for illustrating the basic system. In this specific situation, it has an issue where the way the spell expresses itself in different sub-systems is handled poorly in regards to what makes it &quot;more powerful.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...do I have to spend Reach to do it if whoever wrote the spell thought of something else as a more powerful version of it? </div> </div> </div>Or just house rule that spell if you disagree with the assignment. I mean, how many spells are really sitting there where this is the case? If it's just one or two, is the problem those few spells, or the system? Because I'd arguing it's those spells if that's really the case.<br /> <br /> There's a big difference between, &quot;I disagree with the book's assignment of primary spell factor for this spell,&quot; and, &quot;I want to assign it freely.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if so, shouldn't context matter when considering what is a more powerful version of the spell I want to create for a given situation? </div> </div> </div>No? I mean why should it beyond all the context of the first four steps of Creative Thaumaturgy that you've already gone through (since this includes things like the intent of your spell)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What skill you use to fire a gun isn't a variable you select as part of the process of resolving firing a gun. </div> </div> </div>Except it is.<br /> <br /> If I'm doing a biatholon, and the ST has it as a simple contested roll Athletics roll, I just used Athletics to fire a gun (as well as the rest of the competition).<br /> If I'm hunting and my ST has me roll Survival, I just used Survival to fire a gun to take a deer for some food.<br /> If I'm testing a gun in a lab to study the pattern it leaves on bullets as part of a forensic investigation and I roll Science, I just used Science to fire a gun into a testing tank.<br /> If I'm grappling someone and turn their gun against them to shot them, I just used Brawl to fire a gun.<br /> <br /> This is the connection. While figuring out your dice pool is a simpler process than designing and casting a spell, it still follows the same pattern: you say what you want to do, then you describe how you want to do it, and then you select the traits to roll based on the first two parts, and modify the total based on situation.<br /> <br /> You don't get to say, &quot;I want to harm that guy. I'm going to shot him directly with my drawn gun,&quot; and then not end up rolling Dexterity + Firearms (barring exceptions), because that's the traits you use to follow up the intent and method, even if there are other potential rolls that can be used to resolve a gun being fired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't model anything in the real world, but the mechanics of creative thaumaturgy do model something in the narrative. Namely, the Mage forming an Imago on the fly, as opposed to using an internalized Imago (a Praxis), or memorized Imago (a Rote). </div> </div> </div>And if they form the exact same Imago a second time on the fly, the primary spell factor has no reason to change. If they form a different but similar Imago, it might make sense for a different primary spell factor based on that different Imago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if part of that process is determining what constitutes &quot;a stronger version of that effect&quot;, it feels artificial to me that the Mage formulating the Imago doesn't determine what a stronger version of the spell they are inventing looks like. </div> </div> </div>Because it's not a &quot;stronger version of this specific spell in this specific situation,&quot; it's, &quot;a stronger version of that effect,&quot; and than means that the primary factor was already decided in essence when they picked what the effect was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you can't always make that determination in a vacuum. If you could, there would never be a need to change a spell's Primary Factor. </div> </div> </div>No. You make that determination in the context of the abstract effect of the spell. The want to change any of a spell's factor are done after that determination as part of casting the spell in the context of the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057952#post1057952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my character is improvising a spell, should she not be the one who determines what the spell she improvised is &quot;supposed to do&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. That's literally what the first step of Creative Thaumaturgy is. &quot;What is the intent of the spell.&quot; That's why I keep harping on how the steps of Creative Thaumaturgy are supposed to flow into each other and inform each step in term.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T08:56:17-08:00","id":1058054,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>: Not only is it hidden, but the book provides you with a completely different, subjective criteria for determining Primary Factors. To use your 5e analogy (and you remembered correctly, I both play and DM it), t's like if the rules for creating traps in the dungeon master's guide not only didn't tell you that traps that deal fire damage should deal more than traps that deal damage of another keyword, but also claimed that part of designing a trap was to give it &quot;whatever damage type you immediately think of&quot;, and if players could also use that system to craft their own traps. If there is a secret objective criteria for determining Primary Factor, it's kind of vital for everyone who plays or runs the game to know, it shouldn't be hidden and the book shouldn't provide a misleading alternate criteria. And yeah, same goes for Lasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057955#post1057955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your character is improvising a spell to grant her an abiding view of the immediate future that is distinct from Present As Past, either she is not duplicating Present As Past with the primary factor flipped or she is going to have to contend with the same difficulties of forming an Imago that that spell imposes for that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? If she's the one forming the Imago, why is she not the one who determines the variable of Primary Factor? Why is the criteria not what <i>she</i>, as the spell's creator in-universe, immediately thinks of as a more powerful version of the effect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057955#post1057955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one Reach. The specific spell under discussion in particular is available at a level of Arcanum mastery whose attendant Greater Utility Attainment frees up that same amount of Reach from instant casting. The specific spell under discussion is also not exempt from the normal mechanics allowing the expenditure of Reach for Advanced Duration and references subjects, which rather cuts down on the use of being able to readily make the effect last for multiple weeks. The specific spell under discussion \u2014 and <i>virtually every potential spell this discussion could conceivably apply to</i>, in fact \u2014 is not exempt from the many <i>many</i> ways around the problems that excess Reach presents for a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't care about the 1 Reach cost. That is not and has never been my issue with Primary Factors being fixed. My issue is with the dissonance caused by the subjective criteria for determining an objective quality of the spell. If Primary Factors are supposed to be locked based on the effect of the spell, the book should tell me what it is about an effect that makes it Potency Primary or Duration Primary. If Primary Factors are supposed to be determined by what the creator of the spell thinks would make the effect more powerful, then it should be possible for two otherwise identical spells to have different Primary Factors, because different people are going to immediately think of different ways to make the spell more powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing the disconnect. You can't figure out what you think of a more powerful version of the spell would be if you haven't done the first four steps, and if you do the first four steps the exact same way, the fifth step wouldn't have a reason to produce a different result.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first step of the process is &quot;Declare Intent.&quot; So, if I have a different intent for my spell than the writer of one of the example spells had in mind when they wrote it, then we already haven't done the four steps in the exact same way. And since the criteria given to me for determining Primary Factor is &quot;what I think of as a more powerful version of the spell&quot;, what I intend to accomplish with the spell is going to have a much more significant impact on what I think of as a more powerful version of it than its Arcanum, Practice, Effect and Cost, or Withstand Trait. If I'm supposed to determine it based on something else, the book should have told me that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, can we pick a different example? Present as Past is a distinctly problematic spell on a number of levels that makes it a poor choice for illustrating the basic system. In this specific situation, it has an issue where the way the spell expresses itself in different sub-systems is handled poorly in regards to what makes it &quot;more powerful.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or just house rule that spell if you disagree with the assignment. I mean, how many spells are really sitting there where this is the case? If it's just one or two, is the problem those few spells, or the system? Because I'd arguing it's those spells if that's really the case.<br /> <br /> There's a big difference between, &quot;I disagree with the book's assignment of primary spell factor for this spell,&quot; and, &quot;I want to assign it freely.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the book's assignment of any given spell's primary factor is not my issue. Either the inflexible assignment of Primary Factors based on some unspoken qualities of the spell, or the advice to assign a Primary Factor based on personal feelings is my problem. Either would be fine on its own, but together they create significant cognitive dissonance for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No? I mean why should it beyond all the context of the first four steps of Creative Thaumaturgy that you've already gone through (since this includes things like the intent of your spell)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. So, if the intent of my spell is different than the intent of the writer of the sample spells, should it not be able to have a different Primary Factor?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it is.<br /> <br /> If I'm doing a biatholon, and the ST has it as a simple contested roll Athletics roll, I just used Athletics to fire a gun (as well as the rest of the competition).<br /> If I'm hunting and my ST has me roll Survival, I just used Survival to fire a gun to take a deer for some food.<br /> If I'm testing a gun in a lab to study the pattern it leaves on bullets as part of a forensic investigation and I roll Science, I just used Science to fire a gun into a testing tank.<br /> If I'm grappling someone and turn their gun against them to shot them, I just used Brawl to fire a gun.<br /> <br /> This is the connection. While figuring out your dice pool is a simpler process than designing and casting a spell, it still follows the same pattern: you say what you want to do, then you describe how you want to do it, and then you select the traits to roll based on the first two parts, and modify the total based on situation.<br /> <br /> You don't get to say, &quot;I want to harm that guy. I'm going to shot him directly with my drawn gun,&quot; and then not end up rolling Dexterity + Firearms (barring exceptions), because that's the traits you use to follow up the intent and method, even if there are other potential rolls that can be used to resolve a gun being fired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, fine. But that system for determining dice pools is not player-facing, and the book doesn't advise players to use &quot;whatever they think of as a more powerful dice pool.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they form the exact same Imago a second time on the fly, the primary spell factor has no reason to change. If they form a different but similar Imago, it might make sense for a different primary spell factor based on that different Imago.</div> </div> </div> </div>And is a different intent for the spell not a sufficiently different Imagi to merit a different Primary Factor? If not, why doesn't the book tell me so? This is vital information for me to be able to properly use the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's not a &quot;stronger version of this specific spell in this specific situation,&quot; it's, &quot;a stronger version of that effect,&quot; and than means that the primary factor was already decided in essence when they picked what the effect was.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the book says. It says &quot;<i>what you think of</i> as stronger version of the <i>spell</i>. Since I am using the spell for a specific purpose, what purpose I intend to use the spell for is going to have a significant impact on what I think of as a stronger version of it. If it does not have a significant impact on what you think of as a stronger version, we can already see how two people crafting the same spell might come to different conclusions about what would make it stronger, and by the book's criteria, our spells should then end up with different Primary Factors. And, since Intent is part of crafting a spell, two spells with the same effect but different intent are not identical spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. You make that determination in the context of the abstract effect of the spell. The want to change any of a spell's factor are done after that determination as part of casting the spell in the context of the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the book says. If there's a quality or qualities of the abstract effect of the spell that are supposed to determine the Primary Factor, the book should tell me what they are, instead of telling me &quot;whatever you think will make the spell more powerful.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057965#post1057965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. That's literally what the first step of Creative Thaumaturgy is. &quot;What is the intent of the spell.&quot; That's why I keep harping on how the steps of Creative Thaumaturgy are supposed to flow into each other and inform each step in term.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you saying Intent alone <i>is</i> enough to distinguish a spell, and that two spells with identical effects <i>might</i> have different Primary Factors if their Intent is different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-04-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T09:38:26-08:00","id":1058064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058054#post1058054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? If she's the one forming the Imago, why is she not the one who determines the variable of Primary Factor? Why is the criteria not what <i>she</i>, as the spell's creator in-universe, immediately thinks of as a more powerful version of the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Creative Thaumaturgy rules are not the in-character interface through which your character devises a spell and Supernal magic is not based on in-character subjective assessments. You as a player or Storyteller are devising the mechanics of the spell that the character is assembling through the narrative framework of forming an Imago. Attempting to game the system through selective invocation of the in-character perspective already doesn't produce uncontentious results in these games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My issue is with the dissonance caused by the subjective criteria for determining an objective quality of the spell. If Primary Factors are supposed to be locked based on the effect of the spell, the book should tell me what it is about an effect that makes it Potency Primary or Duration Primary. </div> </div> </div>Again, it seems pretty obvious that spell effects whose nature is to provide a long-term effect is Duration-primary regardless of what scaling Potency does, just as a lot of active Space and Time spells designed to interact with their respective sympathetic systems are Potency-primary even if it would be useful to invoke the history of an object or merge two locations for more than a scene. I don't disagree that the rule could be clearer, but you're not arguing that it should be clearer, you're arguing that the rule <i>shouldn't exist</i>, which is a different matter entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Primary Factors are supposed to be determined by what the creator of the spell thinks would make the effect more powerful, </div> </div> </div><b>They aren't.</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Think of a more powerful version of the spell&quot; is not &quot;Think of what would make the spell 'more powerful,'&quot; else the vast majority of spells' Primary factors would be Potency. A spell that animates a zombie is more powerful if it can be animated for three turns or one week without penalty than that same spell animating a zombie for one turn or one scene without penalty, regardless of the hypothetical existence of a version of the spell that makes a tougher zombie \u2014 Sleeper witnesses may weaken a zombie-animating spell in power or headcount, but the very last thing they will do is cause the spell to end sooner, because a spell that animates a zombie needs to last long enough to allow that zombie to be used for something more than it needs that zombie to be strong enough to do something in particular.<br /> <br /> The Primary Factor is the core boost a spell gets from Arcanum mastery because it's the central factor of the spell's functioning, not because it's a free buff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first step of the process is &quot;Declare Intent.&quot; So, if I have a different intent for my spell than the writer of one of the example spells had in mind when they wrote it, then we already haven't done the four steps in the exact same way. </div> </div> </div>Skipping steps two through four de facto should not give you an otherwise-identical spell, which makes calling it &quot;your&quot; spell exceedingly difficult to not read uncharitably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-04-2017, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T10:28:32-08:00","id":1058078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058064#post1058064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the Creative Thaumaturgy rules are not the in-character interface through which your character devises a spell and Supernal magic is not based on in-character subjective assessments. You as a player or Storyteller are devising the mechanics of the spell that the character is assembling through the narrative framework of forming an Imago. Attempting to game the system through selective invocation of the in-character perspective already doesn't produce uncontentious results in these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine. If I'm the one devising the mechanics of the spell, why am I not the one who determines the variable of Primary Factor? Why is the criteria not what I, as the spell's creator out-of-universe, immediately think of as a more powerful version of the effect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058064#post1058064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, it seems pretty obvious that spell effects whose nature is to provide a long-term effect is Duration-primary regardless of what scaling Potency does, just as a lot of active Space and Time spells designed to interact with their respective sympathetic systems are Potency-primary even if it would be useful to invoke the history of an object or merge two locations for more than a scene. I don't disagree that the rule could be clearer, but you're not arguing that it should be clearer, you're arguing that the rule <i>shouldn't exist</i>, which is a different matter entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may seem obvious to you, but it is not to me. And I am arguing that <i>either</i> the rule should be clearer <i>or</i> it should not exist. I'm fine with either option, but when I am told that the determining factor is whatever I feel makes it more powerful and also that I can't give a sample spell a different primary factor if I disagree about what would make it more powerful, both of these statements cannot be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058064#post1058064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>They aren't.</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Think of a more powerful version of the spell&quot; is not &quot;Think of what would make the spell 'more powerful,'&quot; else the vast majority of spells' Primary factors would be Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing the difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058064#post1058064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell that animates a zombie is more powerful if it can be animated for three turns or one week without penalty than that same spell animating a zombie for one turn or one scene without penalty, regardless of the hypothetical existence of a version of the spell that makes a tougher zombie \u2014 Sleeper witnesses may weaken a zombie-animating spell in power or headcount, but the very last thing they will do is cause the spell to end sooner, because a spell that animates a zombie needs to last long enough to allow that zombie to be used for something more than it needs that zombie to be strong enough to do something in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>A zombie animating spell is a pretty easy one to agree on what would make it more powerful. On the other hand, how about a spell that creates strong winds? Does a more powerful version create stronger winds, or does it create them for longer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058064#post1058064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primary Factor is the core boost a spell gets from Arcanum mastery because it's the central factor of the spell's functioning, not because it's a free buff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the book doesn't give me any insight on how to determine what is a core factor of a spell's functioning, beyond &quot;what you immediately think of&quot;, and when what I immediately think of is not always the same as what the writer of an example spell evidently immediately thought of, it creates a disconnect when the book also tells me that the primary factor for a given effect is always the same. The former suggests it is a subjective quality, the latter suggests it is objective, and I am struggling to reconcile the two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058064#post1058064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skipping steps two through four de facto should not give you an otherwise-identical spell, which makes calling it &quot;your&quot; spell exceedingly difficult to not read uncharitably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I don't always have the inclination to invent a spell from scratch every time? Sometimes I'd rather just work from an example and tweak it slightly to suit my needs. Isn't that why we have example spells in the first place? Well, sometimes an example spell has a different Primary Factor than what I immediately think of as a stronger version of it. And yet I apparently can't use creative thaumaturgy to cast a spell with the same effect but the primary factor I immediately think of. Either the instructions for how to determine primary factor or the provision against creative thaumaturgy producing a spell with the same effect and a different primary factor as one of the examples must not be accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T11:28:25-08:00","id":1058101,"title":"","content":"There seems to be this unspoken consensus on what &quot;stronger&quot; implies, thereby a <b>pre-selection</b> of a Primary Factor that I may not agree with. A stronger version of a zombie control spell COULD have more potency, but the nature of zombies (probably really low resistance) makes Duration the easy choice.<br /> <br /> In cases where it is conceivable to go either longer Duration or higher Potency, the answer is not so clear. The game mechanics ALLOW you to switch after the fact, but you shouldn't have to switch at all if you're using Creative Thaumaturgy to first and foremost DECLARE your own Primary Factor.<br /> <br /> I'm basically just being told &quot;Because THE BOOK SAYS do not design a spell that is identical to a published spell except with a swapped Primary.&quot; Why? Stop telling me it is because the book says, because I am SUPERBLY aware that the book says that.<br /> <br /> My issue is not with spending Reach, either. My problem is with the inherent belief that spells have a predefined lean.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why would you want to start off with a different Primary Factor, that spell is <i>clearly</i> a Duration focused spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why am I forced to start with Potency on some spells, even if I'm designing the Imago? Even if I intend to switch it to the Primary Factor I want anyway. We've established that I'll be using Creative Thaumaturgy, so why not?<br /> <br /> Charlaquin already highlighted many of the most important points, but again, the fact &quot;the book says you can't&quot; underscores a narrative that neither the player or the ST is aware of. A narrative that states &quot;This spell is this Primary Factor for reason X.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's what you immediately think of!--no, it isn't. Why are you assuming that is what I would think of?<br /> <br /> I can't tell why your interpretation of a &quot;More powerful version&quot; is different from mine; moreover, why the &quot;More powerful version&quot; seems to be locked on one particular Primary Factor. (It's just one Reach, who cares, you'll probably end up with more Reaches to spend than you need anyway!--That <b>is not</b> what this discussion is about.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:07:08-08:00","id":1058107,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11166\" data-vbnamecard=\"11166\">kryptonitekrusher</a> Arguments for keeping it the way the book has it spelled out aren't &quot;Just because that's the way the book is.&quot; Instead it's, &quot;Here's a logical argument for why the book is the way it is.&quot; You can disagree with the them if you want, but it'd be nice to not see their position misrepresented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:28:10-08:00","id":1058113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058054#post1058054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>: Not only is it hidden, but the book provides you with a completely different, subjective criteria for determining Primary Factors. To use your 5e analogy (and you remembered correctly, I both play and DM it), t's like if the rules for creating traps in the dungeon master's guide not only didn't tell you that traps that deal fire damage should deal more than traps that deal damage of another keyword, but also claimed that part of designing a trap was to give it &quot;whatever damage type you immediately think of&quot;, and if players could also use that system to craft their own traps. If there is a secret objective criteria for determining Primary Factor, it's kind of vital for everyone who plays or runs the game to know, it shouldn't be hidden and the book shouldn't provide a misleading alternate criteria. And yeah, same goes for Lasting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why? If she's the one forming the Imago, why is she not the one who determines the variable of Primary Factor? Why is the criteria not what <i>she</i>, as the spell's creator in-universe, immediately thinks of as a more powerful version of the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, for authors who spent megaton of hours on the project and breathed it, it probably became so obvious what kind of effect is Primary Duration and what is Primary Potence that it might have looked like it doesn't need any extra explaining. One of Mage's pains is that the book wanted to do so much that it really cut down on presentation and explanations in order to cram more and more content in, kinda like proper explanations and teaching tools are less important than actual rule set. Which is a shame; I feel that RPG games could learn a lot from board games in field of presenting their rules in easily teachable (and learnable) way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:20:26-08:00","id":1058141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058113#post1058113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, for authors who spent megaton of hours on the project and breathed it, it probably became so obvious what kind of effect is Primary Duration and what is Primary Potence that it might have looked like it doesn't need any extra explaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no doubt. This is one of those things that would be great to see clarified in an FAQ like the one Vampire has, but alas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058113#post1058113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of Mage's pains is that the book wanted to do so much that it really cut down on presentation and explanations in order to cram more and more content in, kinda like proper explanations and teaching tools are less important than actual rule set. Which is a shame; I feel that RPG games could learn a lot from board games in field of presenting their rules in easily teachable (and learnable) way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting because there are parts they really did take the time to carefully explain, like how the past is fixed unless changed by magic, the future is constantly in flux, and if you kill your own grandpa in the past you don't poof out of existence but no one in the present has any memory of you. Things that the 1e writers didn't think needed any extra explaining and caused similar confusion. I'm sure if there's ever a 3e, it will explain some things better that 2e failed to, and have some new things it fails to explain. That's just the way it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:42:07-08:00","id":1058177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058107#post1058107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11166\" data-vbnamecard=\"11166\">kryptonitekrusher</a> Arguments for keeping it the way the book has it spelled out aren't &quot;Just because that's the way the book is.&quot; Instead it's, &quot;Here's a logical argument for why the book is the way it is.&quot; You can disagree with the them if you want, but it'd be nice to not see their position misrepresented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, buddy.<br /> <br /> <b>I wouldn't be asking</b> if I agreed with why certain Primary Factor are designated &quot;the default Primary Factor&quot; for any given published spell.<br /> <br /> Satchel is dispensing what he believes to be the &quot;of course it has to be this Primary Factor&quot; when in fact it is not objectively true that a <i>more powerful</i> zombie spell lasts longer. It just isn't, buddy. <br /> <br /> Because &quot;the factor you think of when you think of a stronger version&quot; is dependent on what you intend to do with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:57:55-08:00","id":1058185,"title":"","content":"Imagine that you are monster summoner. Your monster summoner can summon animals and beasts, and their monster summoning ability says that you can summon &quot;stronger&quot;, more &quot;grown up&quot;, &quot;advanced&quot; versions of these base animals. <br /> Just because you need to fly, it doesn't mean that &quot;more powerful tiger&quot; you summon will grow wings. Instead, you will summon giant eagle. <br /> Argument here is that when you cast a spell, you pick an effect from the &quot;list&quot; - just like you pick your animals from summoning zoo list. And just like your summoned animals, spell &quot;seed effects&quot; have natural progression for their &quot;more powerful&quot; forms. You *can* grow wings for your tiger, but it's actively against it's basic nature, so you spend a Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:33:07-08:00","id":1058236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058177#post1058177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, buddy.<br /> <br /> <b>I wouldn't be asking</b> if I agreed with why certain Primary Factor are designated &quot;the default Primary Factor&quot; for any given published spell.<br /> <br /> Satchel is dispensing what he believes to be the &quot;of course it has to be this Primary Factor&quot; when in fact it is not objectively true that a <i>more powerful</i> zombie spell lasts longer. It just isn't, buddy.<br /> <br /> Because &quot;the factor you think of when you think of a stronger version&quot; is dependent on what you intend to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it's fine to disagree, and it's obvious you do. It's rude to misrepresent their position though. It's also rude to be condescending.<br /> <br /> Misrepresenting their position also doesn't make a persuasive argument on your end either, it just makes you appear uninformed or unwilling to pay attention to what's actually being said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T19:50:40-08:00","id":1058261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058236#post1058236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, it's fine to disagree, and it's obvious you do. It's rude to misrepresent their position though. It's also rude to be condescending.<br /> <br /> Misrepresenting their position also doesn't make a persuasive argument on your end either, it just makes you appear uninformed or unwilling to pay attention to what's actually being said.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's really cool and all, but I can also do that trick. I think you appear uninformed or unwilling to pay attention because you're not acknowledging that I do, in fact, acknowledge what they're trying to say and have stated precisely why it is that I disagree with their interpretation.<br /> <br /> You can sit there and act like I only reduced their argument to &quot;because the book says so.&quot; Reducing arguments to what they <b>sound like</b> is not uncommon in this thread, or on these forums; so I don't know what your issue is.<br /> <br /> They've stated that it works as an intended mechanic, it aims to reduce meta-gaming, and that some of the spells mentioned have intuitively apparent Primary Factors (among other arguments.) Those reasons don't mesh with how Creative Thaumaturgy is written when regarding the topic of the thread, so they come off as &quot;that's just the way it is.&quot; If you're unable to see why it looks that way to me, that's cool, but don't twist it into me appearing ignorant. I know what they're trying to say. I'm just communicating how it sounds being repeated over and over again when I, and others, continue to point out that those reasons are not satisfying in-and-of themselves.<br /> <br /> Their argument is not an objectively logical conclusion to me. The fact that you're just telling me it's fine to disagree, when I don't care that we disagree, is absurd. I am aware that we're free to disagree. I don't care what they do in their games. But I'm not buying &quot;zombie spell = Duration, duh.&quot; It doesn't make sense given the subjectiveness of deciding what a spell is intended for unless you generate a narrative for why the default Primary Factors are the way they are.<br /> <br /> I've also proposed circumstances where, for me, the current setup works fine; but it requires me to fill in the blanks because, alone, the Creative Thaumaturgy rules are not satisfying me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T20:22:47-08:00","id":1058277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058078#post1058078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine. If I'm the one devising the mechanics of the spell, why am I not the one who determines the variable of Primary Factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Put bluntly, because in the specific category of situation you're talking about, <i>you aren't devising the mechanics of the spell</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is the criteria not what I, as the spell's creator out-of-universe, immediately think of as a more powerful version of the effect? </div> </div> </div>As WHW goes on to point out, a significant number of spells do not lose fundamental elements of how their effect works just because it's inconvenient for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It may seem obvious to you, but it is not to me. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spell effects that are wholly dependent upon lasting more than a turn like wards or item-creation are Duration-Primary&quot; and &quot;spells with purely immediate effects are Potency-Primary&quot; are both obvious and easily gleaned from the wealth of example spells in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I am arguing that <i>either</i> the rule should be clearer <i>or</i> it should not exist. </div> </div> </div>And the book is already published and has already been out of its errata collection phase for nearly a year, so there is nothing worthwhile that can come of &quot;should&quot; from anyone present. If you want help with interpretation or houserules, there are people on these forums that can help you, but <i>nothing about &quot;should&quot; benefits anything here.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm fine with either option, but when I am told that the determining factor is whatever I feel makes it more powerful and also that I can't give a sample spell a different primary factor if I disagree about what would make it more powerful, both of these statements cannot be true. </div> </div> </div>The rule of &quot;whatever you think of&quot; is explicitly <i>a rule of thumb</i> and the rule of no primary-toggled identical spells is explicitly <i>not </i>\u2014 the self-evident conclusion is then that <i>the rule of thumb bends first</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not seeing the difference. </div> </div> </div>The basic no-frills application of a spell has a quality \u2014 either Potency or Duration \u2014 that distinguishes the work of an Apprentice from the work of a Master even if they're both casting the same spell with no extra Reaches spent or factors accounted for with penalties. Pretty much any factor can make a spell &quot;stronger,&quot; but the primary factor is the backbone of the most basic form of the spell that lets it do what it's supposed to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A zombie animating spell is a pretty easy one to agree on what would make it more powerful. On the other hand, how about a spell that creates strong winds? Does a more powerful version create stronger winds, or does it create them for longer? </div> </div> </div>Are you just generating the Heavy Winds Environmental Tilt? Duration. Are you making a gust of wind that's going to blow at X targets with Y amount of force? Potency. This is what the book is getting at with Declare Intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, but the book doesn't give me any insight on how to determine what is a core factor of a spell's functioning, beyond &quot;what you immediately think of&quot; </div> </div> </div>The Primary Factor gets last priority on Dissonance-induced breakdown and is the factor the spell can have augmented with an exceptional success. Most printed spells bear this out as sufficient reason for their primary factors to be what they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sorry I don't always have the inclination to invent a spell from scratch every time? </div> </div> </div>There's an entire list of Arcanum-agnostic examples between Declare Intent and Primary Factor and there is a world of difference that exists between &quot;I'm taking cues from this example effect&quot; and &quot;I'm literally copying this example effect wholesale and changing the base element of its makeup.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't that why we have example spells in the first place? </div> </div> </div>No, actually. We have example spells to provide examples of the capabilities of specific Arcana as precedent and pre-made effects, much like a college professor might keep copies of exemplary papers from previous students available for your perusal and citation without allowing you to change one paragraph in them and submit the result as your own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either the instructions for how to determine primary factor or the provision against creative thaumaturgy producing a spell with the same effect and a different primary factor as one of the examples must not be accurate. </div> </div> </div>And, lo and behold, the instructions are softer than the provision. The rest is raw complaint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T20:50:25-08:00","id":1058279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put bluntly, because in the specific category of situation you're talking about, <i>you aren't devising the mechanics of the spell</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure I am. The mechanics I've devised just happen to produce the same effect as one of the example spells in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As WHW goes on to point out, a significant number of spells do not lose fundamental elements of how their effect works just because it's inconvenient for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand what you are saying here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Spell effects that are wholly dependent upon lasting more than a turn like wards or item-creation are Duration-Primary&quot; and &quot;spells with purely immediate effects are Potency-Primary&quot; are both obvious and easily gleaned from the wealth of example spells in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? Maybe to you. Not everyone has your aptitude for gleaning such patterns, and to those people it would be nice if the book actually told them these things directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the book is already published and has already been out of its errata collection phase for nearly a year, so there is nothing worthwhile that can come of &quot;should&quot; from anyone present. If you want help with interpretation or houserules, there are people on these forums that can help you, but <i>nothing about &quot;should&quot; benefits anything here.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Believe it or not, I'm aware that the book has already been published and is out of its errata collection phase. I am not attempting to get the book changed. I expressed displeasure with the conflict between the guidelines that are written for how to determine Primary Factor and the disallowing of spells with identical effects but different Primary Factors. I have been met with significant resistance to this position and told all the ways I'm wrong for thinking that. I am at this point merely defending my perspective, because I believe that my frustration with this particular inconsistency is justified. Do I expect the book to be changed? Of course not. But I have the right to be unhappy with the book being stuck the way it is, and to express that dissatisfaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule of &quot;whatever you think of&quot; is explicitly <i>a rule of thumb</i> and the rule of no primary-toggled identical spells is explicitly <i>not </i>\u2014 the self-evident conclusion is then that <i>the rule of thumb bends first</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, but the book doesn't give me any further instructions than the rule of thumb, which as I've said a few times now, is a rather critical thing for people who want to use the system properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic no-frills application of a spell has a quality \u2014 either Potency or Duration \u2014 that distinguishes the work of an Apprentice from the work of a Master even if they're both casting the same spell with no extra Reaches spent or factors accounted for with penalties. Pretty much any factor can make a spell &quot;stronger,&quot; but the primary factor is the backbone of the most basic form of the spell that lets it do what it's supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this have to do with the distinction you implied that exists between &quot;what would make this spell more powerful&quot; and &quot;a more powerful version of this spell&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you just generating the Heavy Winds Environmental Tilt? Duration. Are you making a gust of wind that's going to blow at X targets with Y amount of force? Potency. This is what the book is getting at with Declare Intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting that when I'm talking about a spell whose mechanical effects would seem to suggest Duration primary (Present as Past, to allow more rounds of benefiting from its Initiative manipulation effects), your counter-argument focuses its narrative effect (glimpsing the future), but when I attempt to meet you on those terms and discuss a spell's narrative effect, your counter-argument focuses on the spell's mechanical effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primary Factor gets last priority on Dissonance-induced breakdown and is the factor the spell can have augmented with an exceptional success. Most printed spells bear this out as sufficient reason for their primary factors to be what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>...What?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an entire list of Arcanum-agnostic examples between Declare Intent and Primary Factor and there is a world of difference that exists between &quot;I'm taking cues from this example effect&quot; and &quot;I'm literally copying this example effect wholesale and changing the base element of its makeup.&quot;<br /> <br /> No, actually. We have example spells to provide examples of the capabilities of specific Arcana as precedent and pre-made effects, much like a college professor might keep copies of exemplary papers from previous students available for your perusal and citation without allowing you to change one paragraph in them and submit the result as your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>If an example spell does more or less what I want, I'm not going to bother re-inventing the wheel. Sorry if that bothers you, but I can guarantee I'm not the only person who leans on the example spells in this way. I'm not submitting these spells for publication, I'm just trying to accomplish a particular result in my make-believe-fun-time game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058277#post1058277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, lo and behold, the instructions are softer than the provision. The rest is raw complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relative strength of the instructions and the provision are not my issue, the contradiction between them is. And yes, it is a complaint. It has only ever been a complaint. In case you hadn't noticed, this entire thread has been about a complaint since the opening post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T21:49:46-08:00","id":1058293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058279#post1058279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand what you are saying here.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you need to fly, it doesn't mean that &quot;more powerful tiger&quot; you summon will grow wings. Instead, you will summon giant eagle.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they? Maybe to you. </div> </div> </div>I find it extremely hard to believe that I am in the minority in finding &quot;a spell that makes a thing that's supposed to last is made stronger by lasting longer by default, not by being better by default&quot; an intuitive state of affairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's fine, but the book doesn't give me any further instructions than the rule of thumb, which as I've said a few times now, is a rather critical thing for people who want to use the system properly. </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does this have to do with the distinction you implied that exists between &quot;what would make this spell more powerful&quot; and &quot;a more powerful version of this spell&quot;? </div> </div> </div><i>Every additive spell factor</i> makes a spell &quot;more powerful,&quot; which is why they incur penalties or cost Reach. The primary factor is the stable point of scaling efficaciousness for a spell, which is the fundamental difference between <i>a version of Dispel Magic cast by an Apprentice</i> and <i>a version of Dispel Magic cast by a Master</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's interesting that when I'm talking about a spell whose mechanical effects would seem to suggest Duration primary (Present as Past, to allow more rounds of benefiting from its Initiative manipulation effects), your counter-argument focuses its narrative effect (glimpsing the future), but when I attempt to meet you on those terms and discuss a spell's narrative effect, your counter-argument focuses on the spell's mechanical effect. </div> </div> </div>It is indeed very interesting that when I bring up the distinction between making a gust of wind to make an area windy and making a gust of wind to move things this is suddenly more of a relevant mechanical distinction than a spell effect that can be re-cast every turn without disjunction and becomes available at the same level as an Attainment that saves you a Reach on Instant casting, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...What? </div> </div> </div>The Primary Factor is not just &quot;add X steps to this factor for free&quot; and the qualities of the primary factor that are not the free levels can be looked at as sufficient reason to have most spells keep their primary factors as they are even if the Primary Factor added no levels to anything on its own. Rolling well allows free steps or Reaches in the primary factor, and a spell that is subject to Dissonance loses ranks in its primary factor last before it is destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everyone has your aptitude for gleaning such patterns, and to those people it would be nice if the book actually told them these things directly. </div> </div> </div>It would also be nice if people would refrain from pointing to my ostensible expertise \u2014 a quality which I will readily inform you is the product of just going through the books comprehensively, keeping prior material in mind, and endeavoring to synthesize a reading that makes sense \u2014 as an excuse to throw my interpretations back in my face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I have the right to be unhappy with the book being stuck the way it is, and to express that dissatisfaction. </div> </div> </div>And you've done so multiple times now. Other people disagreeing with your dissatisfaction does not negate that expression, nor is their disagreement an infringement upon that right, nor does expression of either dissatisfaction or disagreement amount to much of any worth in a forum for discussing and asking questions about the game. I can <i>do something</i> about questions, because that is one of the main reasons I actually read the books despite the relative scarcity of gaming groups in my neck of the woods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, it is a complaint. It has only ever been a complaint. In case you hadn't noticed, this entire thread has been about a complaint since the opening post. </div> </div> </div>Yes. It would be nice if I didn't have half the reason I've been going through the games' older material in order \u2014 to be able to be a helpful resource for the community because I enjoy these games and would like to be able to help other people enjoy them \u2014 put through the shredder because people's feelings that I cannot do anything about mean I'm wasting my time attempting to engage with the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> I'm a reader. A moderately competent one, yes, but I can do nothing to help with repeated complaints about not liking the way a system works, and <i>that is the entire conceit of Johnny's thread here </i>aside from the request for justifications that's looking increasingly like a perfunctory show of interest. I'll readily step out if the only real purpose of this thread is to keep hammering at the ambiguity of the rule of thumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-05-2017, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T22:03:25-08:00","id":1058296,"title":"","content":"Satchel, I don't mean to sound rude (and I'm sorry if it ends up coming out that way), but have you ever been told that you have a very distinct way of communicating?<br /> <br /> I say that because I have to read and re-read your posts all the time. I consider myself a pretty apt reader, but ... pardon the colloquial expression --- you be on the next level, LOL.<br /> <br /> Perfunctory? Efficaciousness?<br /> <br /> I know, I know, Google it--but seriously, I don't know if it helps the situation if the person trying to understand you needs to understand your writing in order to understand what your point about the topic at hand is.<br /> <br /> When Charlaquin said <i>&quot;... What?&quot;</i> I laughed out loud because I also said that.<br /> <br /> I'm literally sitting here reading your posts and asking myself if I'm retarded and you're actually saying something really easy to understand ... or if you're repeating what I think you've already said in different ways and I still disagree.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T22:32:56-08:00","id":1058299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it extremely hard to believe that I am in the minority in finding &quot;a spell that makes a thing that's supposed to last is made stronger by lasting longer by default, not by being better by default&quot; an intuitive state of affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know as it matters if you're in the minority or not. That a significant number of people find these implications difficult to ascertain is enough to establish that more clarity would be beneficial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Every additive spell factor</i> makes a spell &quot;more powerful,&quot; which is why they incur penalties or cost Reach. The primary factor is the stable point of scaling efficaciousness for a spell, which is the fundamental difference between <i>a version of Dispel Magic cast by an Apprentice</i> and <i>a version of Dispel Magic cast by a Master</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting warmer, but I'm still not sure how this information helps me reconcile &quot;your personal assessment of what constitutes a more powerful version of this spell is the determining criteria for Primary Factor&quot; with &quot;a given effect only has one possible primary factor.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is indeed very interesting that when I bring up the distinction between making a gust of wind to make an area windy and making a gust of wind to move things this is suddenly more of a relevant mechanical distinction than a spell effect that can be re-cast every turn without disjunction and becomes available at the same level as an Attainment that saves you a Reach on Instant casting, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lost me. And I thought you were arguing that the effect, not the intended use of the effect, was what mattered? Now you're talking about what I'm making gusts of winds to do, which sounds like intent to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primary Factor is not just &quot;add X steps to this factor for free&quot; and the qualities of the primary factor that are not the free levels can be looked at as sufficient reason to have most spells keep their primary factors as they are even if the Primary Factor added no levels to anything on its own. Rolling well allows free steps or Reaches in the primary factor, and a spell that is subject to Dissonance loses ranks in its primary factor last before it is destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>O... Kay... look, you don't need you to convince me that there are good reasons for Primary Factors to be locked-in based on spell effects. I'm fine with that being the case, on the condition that I be given the necessary tools to evaluate what a given effect's Primary Factor should be. As it stands, the only tools I've been given are &quot;do what you feel is right&quot; and &quot;thoroughly analyze every spell in the book and figure out the pattern for yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also be nice if people would refrain from pointing to my ostensible expertise \u2014 a quality which I will readily inform you is the product of just going through the books comprehensively, keeping prior material in mind, and endeavoring to synthesize a reading that makes sense \u2014 as an excuse to throw my interpretations back in my face.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be less of a problem for you if you weren't constantly using that expertise to condescend others' lack of expertise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you've done so multiple times now. Other people disagreeing with your dissatisfaction does not negate that expression, nor is their disagreement an infringement upon that right, nor does expression of either dissatisfaction or disagreement amount to much of any worth in a forum for discussing and asking questions about the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, sometimes people just want to air their grievances in peace. That can be useful discussion in and of itself. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058293#post1058293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can <i>do something</i> about questions, because that is one of the main reasons I actually read the books despite the relative scarcity of gaming groups in my neck of the woods.<br /> <br /> Yes. It would be nice if I didn't have half the reason I've been going through the games' older material in order \u2014 to be able to be a helpful resource for the community because I enjoy these games and would like to be able to help other people enjoy them \u2014 put through the shredder because people's feelings that I cannot do anything about mean I'm wasting my time attempting to engage with the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> I'm a reader. A moderately competent one, yes, but I can do nothing to help with repeated complaints about not liking the way a system works, and <i>that is the entire conceit of Johnny's thread here </i>aside from the request for justifications that's looking increasingly like a perfunctory show of interest. I'll readily step out if the only real purpose of this thread is to keep hammering at the ambiguity of the rule of thumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to help, leave the passive aggression at the door and share the knowledge you've gleaned from all this reading in words one doesn't have to be an English graduate to parse. I've been saying all along that one of the ways to resolve this issue to my satisfaction would be properly explaining objective criteria for assessing whether an effect is Potency Primary or Duration Primary. But instead of doing the helpful thing and walking me through a step-by-step process of assessing the proper Primary Factor for a spell, you've chosen at every turn to poke holes in my posts and tell me why I'm wrong for wanting to resolve a perceived incongruity in the rules in the manner that requires the least amount of work on my part. You're engaging me like a debate partner, not like a guide, so I can't exactly be blamed for reading your intent as being to discredit my position rather than to help me better understand the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-05-2017, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T23:25:20-08:00","id":1058306,"title":"","content":"If a spell has an immediate effect, it's Potency-primary. If a spell has a prolonged effect, it's Duration-primary. <br /> Making an immediate-effect spell repeat itself from lengthened Duration is inherently more complex, so it needs a Reach. <br /> Making a prolonged-effect spell flare strongly with increased Potency, but burn out quickly due to lack of Duration defeats the purpose of the spell, thus it requires more mental effort represented as Reach to justify a spell working like that. <br /> <br /> The above sentences are both my interpretation of the primary factor rules, and what Satchel seems to be trying to convey (but apparently without much success, as usual).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T01:07:57-08:00","id":1058321,"title":"","content":"I kinda wonder if there is actually anything other than required effort (and effort-to-profit formula) stopping OPP from going next level and actually patching their books. I mean, they are digital anyway and any change you make will be literally updated on the drivethru and emailed to people with &quot;hey, Mage core is 1.02 now! Happy mageing!&quot;<br /> But that's a side thought. Voicing critique and dissatisfaction with elements of work is always more productive than listing positive qualities of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T01:37:28-08:00","id":1058323,"title":"","content":"I'd wager there's a large influence of people that buy the PoD copies of the books not wanting to have to buy the book again. So there would need to be the added effort to make sure people that already have a physical copy (and generally prefer using the physical copy) will get simple access to any changes.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be hard to include a change-log style pdf to print that's free whenever that happens, but it's more effort than just updating the main pdf in DTRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:24:10-08:00","id":1058356,"title":"","content":"Also the writers are working on other stuff and don't get paid for updates to the rules that you don't pay for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:06:43-08:00","id":1058456,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> ,not to turn this into a discussion about Satchel's posting habits, but<br /> <br /> A) we all know that there is a tendency for minorities to be vocal, unless we've forgotten Humanist Promethean and Traditional Descent arguments and their like already. A platform is not the same thing as a majority.<br /> B) we have tons of examples of Satchel merely expositing on a subject versus where he is knocking on someone, and it's not particularly fair to treat any time he is explaining something in depth as him condescending to the other party merely because he is being loquacious. In this case, it's also worth remembering that others are shooting first.<br /> <br /> As regards the actual conversation, I feel like there's this misunderstanding going on in regards to magic, namely that magic is not wholly in your control. This is not a power that is merely a river, it has a nature and texture(and possibly a will, if you believe the Mysterium) that requires some carving. Primary Factor is not a thing that is shaped in response to intent any more than a flower is-it responds to the &quot;environment&quot; it exists within. There's a geography to this thing that mages have to change and mold into their vision-hell, that's the entire point of spellcasting.<br /> <br /> I might have more to say on this later-but as for now, kindly remember that magic is more like a serpent and less like a river.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:54:52-08:00","id":1058508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058321#post1058321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wonder if there is actually anything other than required effort (and effort-to-profit formula) stopping OPP from going next level and actually patching their books. I mean, they are digital anyway and any change you make will be literally updated on the drivethru and emailed to people with &quot;hey, Mage core is 1.02 now! Happy mageing!&quot;<br /> But that's a side thought. Voicing critique and dissatisfaction with elements of work is always more productive than listing positive qualities of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Voicing a &quot;critique&quot; does not give you the right to have your conplaints agreed with, much much much less &quot;patched&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:26:01-08:00","id":1058572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058456#post1058456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As regards the actual conversation, I feel like there's this misunderstanding going on in regards to magic, namely that magic is not wholly in your control. This is not a power that is merely a river, it has a nature and texture(and possibly a will, if you believe the Mysterium) that requires some carving. Primary Factor is not a thing that is shaped in response to intent any more than a flower is-it responds to the &quot;environment&quot; it exists within. There's a geography to this thing that mages have to change and mold into their vision-hell, that's the entire point of spellcasting.<br /> <br /> I might have more to say on this later-but as for now, kindly remember that magic is more like a serpent and less like a river.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's a misunderstanding going on as to the nature of the grievance with the whole primary factor thing. For me at least, I don't have a problem with primary factors being fixed based on the effects of a spell <i>per se</i>. My problem is that the guidelines for determining primary factor subjective. It's &quot;what you think of&quot; and different people are going to think of different things. For me, either more specific, objectice guidelines on how to determine a spell's primary factor or more flexibility on what primary factors a spell might have would fix the problem. Explaining to me why primary factors should be locked in, whether from a mechanical perspective or a lore perspective, will not resolve this issue for me because no matter how sold I am on &quot;primary factors should be fixed&quot;, this won't change the lack of guidelines for how to determine Primary Factor.<br /> <br /> I went after the inability to change Primary Factors with creative Thaumaturgy originally because it's the path of least resistance for me to resolve the cognitive dissonance I am having between primary factors being objective and the guidelines for determining them being subjective. Rather than try to dissect the spellcasting system and figure out the unspoken rules of what makes a spell Duration Primary or Potency Primary, I can just say &quot;Creative Thaum can be used to change primary factors in my game&quot; and have it done with. Through all of this, though, only one person has offered more specific guidelines for determining primary factors, the other thing I have repeatedly said would resolve this issue for me. Or, apparently two people, but Satchel's attempts to do so did not come across that way to me at all.<br /> <br /> Rather than talking about Magic being like a snake or a river, what would be helpful to me is for someone to tell me how to figure out based on a spell's effect whether it should be Potency Primary or Duration Primary. WHW got that, but didn't go so far as to actually offer an explanation. So far I've got &quot;instantaneous effects tend to be Potency Primary, efects that apply continuously for a finite Duration tend to be Duration Primary.&quot; Is there anything else I should add to those guidelines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:34:30-08:00","id":1058574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058572#post1058572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far I've got &amp;quot;instantaneous effects tend to be Potency Primary, efects that apply continuously for a finite Duration tend to be Duration Primary.&amp;quot; Is there anything else I should add to those guidelines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the only thing that matters? Might've have to review the book, but that certainly sounds like the prime criterion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:38:55-08:00","id":1058580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058574#post1058574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that the only thing that matters? Might've have to review the book, but that certainly sounds like the prime criterion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so what about Analyze Life? It seems from my reading to have an instantaneous one-off effect, but its Primary Factor is Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:48:46-08:00","id":1058581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058580#post1058580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so what about Analyze Life? It seems from my reading to have an instantaneous one-off effect, but its Primary Factor is Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will continue to update you with current information from the subject while you study them. It doesn't have any Potency based effects since it's front loaded, so Duration is its primary factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:53:36-08:00","id":1058582,"title":"","content":"How about Reading the Outermost Eddies? It hangs over its subject for the Duration and does nothing if the Duration expires before the Blessing or Curse kicks in, but is Potency Primary. Or Exceptional Luck, which apllies a Boon or Bane to the subject for the Duration, but is Potency Primary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-05-2017, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:56:11-08:00","id":1058583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058580#post1058580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so what about Analyze Life? It seems from my reading to have an instantaneous one-off effect, but its Primary Factor is Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, things like that remind me that I don't live in a perfect world. <br /> <br /> Mrmdubois has a working explanation up there, though. Maybe we should add his second sentence as another criterion? Would that turn up further inconsistencies, or help resolve them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:59:30-08:00","id":1058585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058582#post1058582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Reading the Outermost Eddies? It hangs over its subject for the Duration and does nothing if the Duration expires before the Blessing or Curse kicks in, but is Potency Primary. Or Exceptional Luck, which apllies a Boon or Bane to the subject for the Duration, but is Potency Primary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel all Fate spells that arrange for fortune in the future have that &quot;Well, that's all I can do for now- feel free to call me later!&quot; thing going on, regardless of whether it is better being forceful or enduring.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I think boons and hexes are usually meant to take in effect right now, so that you have a lucky moment rather than a lucky day, the latter which will of course require more magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:59:53-08:00","id":1058586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058582#post1058582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Reading the Outermost Eddies? It hangs over its subject for the Duration and does nothing if the Duration expires before the Blessing or Curse kicks in, but is Potency Primary. Or Exceptional Luck, which apllies a Boon or Bane to the subject for the Duration, but is Potency Primary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both of those spells have to overcome Withstand if used in a hostile fashion. Spells that have to overcome Withstand are Potency primary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:00:11-08:00","id":1058587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058572#post1058572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's a misunderstanding going on as to the nature of the grievance with the whole primary factor thing. For me at least, I don't have a problem with primary factors being fixed based on the effects of a spell <i>per se</i>. My problem is that the guidelines for determining primary factor subjective. It's &quot;what you think of&quot; and different people are going to think of different things. For me, either more specific, objectice guidelines on how to determine a spell's primary factor or more flexibility on what primary factors a spell might have would fix the problem. Explaining to me why primary factors should be locked in, whether from a mechanical perspective or a lore perspective, will not resolve this issue for me because no matter how sold I am on &quot;primary factors should be fixed&quot;, this won't change the lack of guidelines for how to determine Primary Factor.<br /> <br /> I went after the inability to change Primary Factors with creative Thaumaturgy originally because it's the path of least resistance for me to resolve the cognitive dissonance I am having between primary factors being objective and the guidelines for determining them being subjective. Rather than try to dissect the spellcasting system and figure out the unspoken rules of what makes a spell Duration Primary or Potency Primary, I can just say &quot;Creative Thaum can be used to change primary factors in my game&quot; and have it done with. Through all of this, though, only one person has offered more specific guidelines for determining primary factors, the other thing I have repeatedly said would resolve this issue for me. Or, apparently two people, but Satchel's attempts to do so did not come across that way to me at all.<br /> <br /> Rather than talking about Magic being like a snake or a river, what would be helpful to me is for someone to tell me how to figure out based on a spell's effect whether it should be Potency Primary or Duration Primary. WHW got that, but didn't go so far as to actually offer an explanation. So far I've got &quot;instantaneous effects tend to be Potency Primary, efects that apply continuously for a finite Duration tend to be Duration Primary.&quot; Is there anything else I should add to those guidelines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, remember that I'm not an english native speaker and my english aptitude comes from watching Cartoon Network and playing games in english when I was in primary school, so I don't feel comfortable trying to explain something so complicated. That's why I nudged Heavy Arms to give it a shot in one of earlier posts. But I guess I'll try:<br /> <br /> - If a spell is naturally lasting, like healing or damaging spells, it's going to be Potency primary. I don't think there are any Duration Primary spells that would repeat on Ritual Interval rate.<br /> So *if a spell would be something that repeats on Ritual Intervals, it will almost never be a Duration Primary spell*. This is also why a lot of people look at Primary Factor when trying to guess if spell was intended to be Lasting or not. <br /> <br /> -If spells function isn't something that takes place immediately, and it's basic concept requires it to stick around for more than a blink of an eye, it will be probably Duration Primary. That's why Zombie Spell is Duration Primary - sure, BIGGER STRONGER FASTER SMARTER zombie is great, but there is no point having Super Hulkbuster Zombie for 3 seconds, isn't there? This is why spells that generally create something - this can be an item, a creature, or a bond - are generally Duration Primary.if you want more evocative reason for this, the &quot;biggest miracle&quot; of these spells usually isn't how strong the effect they conjure is; it's the fact that alas, the body started walking again! Making it little stronger is in no comparison to the fact that dead walk again!! Or something. I'm not good at evocative writing. Fireball is measured by how strong the fires are; obtaining ability to command fires is measured against how long you can sustain this effect, with &quot;what is the biggest fire I can command&quot; being secondary question.<br /> <br /> - If a spell bestows upon the subject a new quality - like a new skill, ability to control something, or so on - it's usually Duration Primary, because again, how strong is the skill you gained is secondary to the fact that you gained the skill.<br /> <br /> - If a spell primarly operates against Clash of Wills - like a lot of shielding spells (though &quot;shielding&quot; in general also falls under above criteria) do - it will be Duration Primary, because Duration also represents how tenacious the spell is and how deeply it roots itself in the Fallen World. <br /> <br /> - If a spell flat out doesn't work when stopped by Withstand - like Sever Soul - it might be Potency Primary, though this is a slippery measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:01:47-08:00","id":1058589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058583#post1058583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mrmdubois has a working explanation up there, though. Maybe we should add his second sentence as another criterion? Would that turn up further inconsistencies, or help resolve them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not spelled out very well in the spell, but it's apparent that though all the information is delivered immediately that it's supposed to be able to keep on updating you or there would be no need for it to mention studying the subject of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:04:23-08:00","id":1058590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058586#post1058586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of those spells have to overcome Withstand if used in a hostile fashion. Spells that have to overcome Withstand are Potency primary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so that's one to add to the list of criteria. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058587#post1058587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, remember that I'm not an english native speaker and my english aptitude comes from watching Cartoon Network and playing games in english when I was in primary school, so I don't feel comfortable trying to explain something so complicated. That's why I nudged Heavy Arms to give it a shot in one of earlier posts. But I guess I'll try:<br /> <br /> - If a spell is naturally lasting, like healing or damaging spells, it's going to be Potency primary. I don't think there are any Duration Primary spells that would repeat on Ritual Interval rate.<br /> So *if a spell would be something that repeats on Ritual Intervals, it will almost never be a Duration Primary spell*. This is also why a lot of people look at Primary Factor when trying to guess if spell was intended to be Lasting or not. <br /> <br /> -If spells function isn't something that takes place immediately, and it's basic concept requires it to stick around for more than a blink of an eye, it will be probably Duration Primary. That's why Zombie Spell is Duration Primary - sure, BIGGER STRONGER FASTER SMARTER zombie is great, but there is no point having Super Hulkbuster Zombie for 3 seconds, isn't there? This is why spells that generally create something - this can be an item, a creature, or a bond - are generally Duration Primary.if you want more evocative reason for this, the &amp;quot;biggest miracle&amp;quot; of these spells usually isn't how strong the effect they conjure is; it's the fact that alas, the body started walking again! Making it little stronger is in no comparison to the fact that dead walk again!! Or something. I'm not good at evocative writing. Fireball is measured by how strong the fires are; obtaining ability to command fires is measured against how long you can sustain this effect, with &amp;quot;what is the biggest fire I can command&amp;quot; being secondary question.<br /> <br /> - If a spell bestows upon the subject a new quality - like a new skill, ability to control something, or so on - it's usually Duration Primary, because again, how strong is the skill you gained is secondary to the fact that you gained the skill.<br /> <br /> - If a spell primarly operates against Clash of Wills - like a lot of shielding spells (though &amp;quot;shielding&amp;quot; in general also falls under above criteria) do - it will be Duration Primary, because Duration also represents how tenacious the spell is and how deeply it roots itself in the Fallen World. <br /> <br /> - If a spell flat out doesn't work when stopped by Withstand - like Sever Soul - it might be Potency Primary, though this is a slippery measure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much. This has been the single most helpful post to me in the entire thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:05:08-08:00","id":1058591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058589#post1058589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not spelled out very well in the spell, but it's apparent that though all the information is delivered immediately that it's supposed to be able to keep on updating you or there would be no need for it to mention studying the subject of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a doctor in diagnosis? Interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:09:46-08:00","id":1058595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1058589#post1058589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not spelled out very well in the spell, but it's apparent that though all the information is delivered immediately that it's supposed to be able to keep on updating you or there would be no need for it to mention studying the subject of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, for a comparison look at Pierce Deception and Know Nature. Know Nature is instant &quot;burst&quot; of information - thus it's Potency Primary. Pierce Deception is &quot;an enhancement that allows you to detect lies&quot;, basically &quot;updating&quot; you with new information like Analyze Life, so they are Duration Primary - their biggest boon is bestowing a new ongoing ability on you.<br /> <br /> There are some tricky spells, like Platonic Form, but I guess Platonic Form being Potency Primary is because the spell conceptually sacrifices &quot;lastingness&quot; - items created by it are short lived and their lifespan is determined by their Mana capacity (and thus potency) more than actual Duration. In comparison, Shadow Crafting has no &quot;destroy after X uses&quot; clause, and thus is Duration Primary. Shadow Form spell probably would look a lot like Platonic Form with Potency Primary being included in it, while Platonic Crafting would probably be a palette swap of Shadow Crafting, with Duration being primary.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:32:10-08:00","id":1059035,"title":"","content":"I'm less sour about this rule than I was when I originally posted my complaint, but I still feel it takes a little of the &quot;creative&quot; out of creative thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> For instance, if I create a spell that isn't in the book I can do whatever I want, but if a spell that I want is different only in Primary factor and it's in the book, then I can't do it without spending the Reach. That doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> If there were firmer guidelines like the ones WHW is proposing I would be more supportive of the rule as there would be OBJECTIVE criteria for determining the Primary factor of a spell, not just &quot;whatever you think of when you think of a more powerful version&quot;, which is very subjective and leads to arguments at the table and thus less fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:24:30-08:00","id":1059116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1057952#post1057952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's made with creative thaumaturgy. By the book's own description, a spell is either a Rote, a Praxis, or improvised. If my character is improvising a spell, should she not be the one who determines what the spell she improvised is &quot;supposed to do&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that you have said a few times here, and even more so when you said 'casting with Creative Thaumaturgy'. And something that I think will help clear up some of the confusion about which Factor is Primary for a given spell. Others have started providing actual criteria, but i feel like this is a metaphysical note that needs to be made.<br /> <br /> Creative Thaumaturgy and Improvised Casting are not the same thing. Creative Thaumaturgy is the alternative to using printed spells; regardless of if those are then used as a Rote, Praxis or Improvised. It is a wholly out of character thing. Mage's don't concisously pick the primary Factor in character, they just construct an Imago with the effects they want. At the very first instance of that Imago forming they will have naturally envisioned either a hard hitting spell or a long lasting one (using the guidelines that WHW posted before), if they want to change that it takes effort (Reach). So when writing a spell out of character, you have to decide what is most likley to come to mind when a spell 'effect' is decided upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:28:26-08:00","id":1059119,"title":"","content":"I'm of unpopular opinion that limitations breed creativity and endless freedom is the worst thing for it, so I don't mind not being able to freely create anything I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:59:19-08:00","id":1059141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1059035#post1059035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm less sour about this rule than I was when I originally posted my complaint, but I still feel it takes a little of the &quot;creative&quot; out of creative thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> For instance, if I create a spell that isn't in the book I can do whatever I want, but if a spell that I want is different only in Primary factor and it's in the book, then I can't do it without spending the Reach. That doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> If there were firmer guidelines like the ones WHW is proposing I would be more supportive of the rule as there would be OBJECTIVE criteria for determining the Primary factor of a spell, not just &quot;whatever you think of when you think of a more powerful version&quot;, which is very subjective and leads to arguments at the table and thus less fun.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe people have been trying to tell me you <b>should not</b> decide Primary Factor without applying the Potency/Duration rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> The game system is trusting you to use better judgment, because it doesn't necessarily word it like the ST is meant to intervene and restructure your spell for you if it doesn't sound right.<br /> <br /> Basically, when you declare the spell, &quot;I want to heal this person.&quot; That very initial statement, during the Creative Thaumaturgy process, constitutes Potency before anything else.<br /> <br /> However, you are allowed to modify it with &quot;I want to heal this person. - Continuously.&quot; At which point you would switch the factor over with a Reach. You've taken your base function, your root, and modified it. The confusion seems to stem from the belief that you're 100% free to declare it however way you want, but I think the book wants you to apply the rule of them whenever possible. It wants you to apply the rule of thumb ALWAYS for published spells because the writers of those spells have already determined the root function for you.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The intent, as I see it, is to declare the root function of the spell as the Primary Factor. No matter what the spell is, you should always strive to narrow the spells intent to some really basic function and use that as your Primary Factor.<br /> <br /> I presume that if you assign Primary Factor by the rule of thumb for every circumstance, regardless of whether or not the spell is published, you'll probably get to a conclusion that doesn't sound contradictory.<br /> <br /> I think the reason it isn't a 100% bonafide ruling is because spells can be really complicated and the work of deciding the root cause can be difficult. However, that work is already done for you in the published spells. Ergo, you shouldn't tweak them if you're applying the universal rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: The rule of thumb I'm referring to is what 21C Hermit spoke of when they said in an earlier post:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If a spell has an immediate effect, it's Potency-primary. If a spell has a prolonged effect, it's Duration-primary.<br /> Making an immediate-effect spell repeat itself from lengthened Duration is inherently more complex, so it needs a Reach.<br /> Making a prolonged-effect spell flare strongly with increased Potency, but burn out quickly due to lack of Duration defeats the purpose of the spell, thus it requires more mental effort represented as Reach to justify a spell working like that.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I think the other rule - &quot;whichever you think of when contemplating a stronger version&quot; - is a tool to zero in on the root function of your spell so you can go back to the rule of thumb and continue as per normal. Meaning you apply the second rule when applying the first rule isn't clear, if I understand correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 03-06-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:13:04-08:00","id":1059149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1059141#post1059141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe people have been trying to tell me you <b>should not</b> decide Primary Factor without applying the Potency/Duration rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> The game system is trusting you to use better judgment, because it doesn't necessarily word it like the ST is meant to intervene and restructure your spell for you if it doesn't sound right.<br /> <br /> Basically, when you declare the spell, &quot;I want to heal this person.&quot; That very initial statement, during the Creative Thaumaturgy process, constitutes Potency before anything else.<br /> <br /> However, you are allowed to modify it with &quot;I want to heal this person. - Continuously.&quot; At which point you would switch the factor over with a Reach. You've taken your base function, your root, and modified it. The confusion seems to stem from the belief that you're 100% free to declare it however way you want, but I think the book wants you to apply the rule of them whenever possible. It wants you to apply the rule of thumb ALWAYS for published spells because the writers of those spells have already determined the root function for you.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could improvise a spell that looks and works differently towards &quot;healing a person over a period of time&quot; than a Ritual Interval Repeating heal spell. Something that, perhaps, gives them a Condition that heals them over time, or increases their natural healing, or regenerates them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:33:18-08:00","id":1059166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1059149#post1059149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could improvise a spell that looks and works differently towards &quot;healing a person over a period of time&quot; than a Ritual Interval Repeating heal spell. Something that, perhaps, gives them a Condition that heals them over time, or increases their natural healing, or regenerates them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at that point I think your root function is <b>a condition</b> that applies healing/regen.<br /> <br /> If it is in the book, such a spell would be Duration Primary anyway. (I haven't checked.)<br /> <br /> Working backwards, you could also state I want to apply <b>a condition</b> that heals, and then switch with a Reach into Potency to maximize healing instead of duration.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:03:14-08:00","id":1059189,"title":"","content":"The Duration Primary spell Body Control halves the healing time for every Potency. However, the increased healing is just one out of many effects that spell grants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T13:12:12-08:00","id":1158262,"title":"","content":"I still encounter way too many examples of spells in the book that have messed up Primary factors. I still believe a lot of it was done for balance reasons, not because it makes sense flavor wise.<br /> <br /> Like Honing the Form: Clearly when you think of a spell that increases your Strength, you would think that Potency (literally a word for Strength) should be the Primary factor, but they made it Duration in the book purely for balance reasons.<br /> <br /> The main culprit is that Advanced Duration is a whole Scene even at Level 1. This way they force you to use 2 Reach to get what makes sense.<br /> <br /> Btw, Augment the Mind is Potency Primary. LOL No consistency.<br /> <br /> Or Wards &amp; Signs. Clearly a better Ward is a more Potent Ward. It's just a power speed bump to make it Duration.<br /> <br /> I've decided to house rule that if the player can make a reasonable case for it they can change it without Reach, but that it has to be chosen and hard-coded for Rotes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T15:33:58-08:00","id":1158289,"title":"","content":"Remember that the arcana were written by different authors, so consistency would suffer just from that although I'm sure they tried to keep it as consistent. The author of Honing the Form and the like probably had a reason they thought Duration made more sense, but if Potency does make more sense, just switch it to that as the usual Primary factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T15:41:36-08:00","id":1158290,"title":"","content":"I thought honing the form was duration because you don't want it to end in three seconds....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T16:35:12-08:00","id":1158295,"title":"","content":"It has bothered me that augment mind is potency but honing the form is duration. I wonder if that was missed or justified during the process of applying errata to the final version of our books.<br /> <br /> I remember when Birth Spirit was Potency instead of Duration. I'm glad they errata'd that, it was such a huge disconnect between me and my ex-ST.<br /> <br /> If I had to hazard a guess, if you want a stronger body, you want it strong for a long time because you're not sure when you'll need that strength? But if you need a stronger mind or social skills, you'll know precisely when the situation has arisen because the time is <i>now</i> at the time of casting, and now its time to boost your mind and you won't need that mental strength so much during the down-time when the scene is done.<br /> <br /> But I'm not satisfied with my own explanation. I think all buff spells should be duration, if for no other reason that, speaking in the meta, it makes the spell less spammy, and rewards mages who plan and prepare instead of impulsive mages. But that's just a ST preference of mine--I like mages being at their strongest when they plan and prepare.<br /> <br /> And this is also why I feel that the +reach option for switching primary spellfactors is an interesting one. It <i>is</i> a roadblock. It absolutely is. <i>It absolutely is</i>.<br /> <br /> But <i>when</i> is it a roadblock? Well, typically its a roadblock when you've <i>run into a niche situation where the normal version of the spell isn't quite as good.</i> This is a rare situation. Its a rare situation where your mage is caught off-guard. So how do you get back ontop? By doubling back, preparing, find a way around your limitations, around your roadblock, by spending extra time and care (and reach) into making a sub<i>-</i>optimal spell that will do the job better <i>this way</i> at <i>this time</i> despite it being unorthodox. This feels very Mage-ey to me.<br /> <br /> The heuristic of when the primary spellfactor feels appropriate is deeefinitely weird to me too, though. There are some spells where the primary spellfactor feels arbitrary. In these situations I think it should either be homeruled or left up to the player based on the Mage's magical style--but it should remain consistent after-that-point.<br /> <br /> If the stronger faster zombie or the Hone the Form spell being Potency primary spellfactor feels right to your mage player, then that might <i>be</i> true for <i>that</i> Mage. But it will probably lock them into it--overcoming their biases and instincts for magic to rewire their instinctive expectations for a spell by using reach? Sounds interesting to me, sounds lore-friendly to me.<br /> <br /> This has been such an interesting thread...!<br /> I hope my contribution isn't too uh... haphazard or uninteresting...<br /> <br /> <br /> I did have a minor example for something like this, where you meta a pre-existing spell a bit to get the same effect but with different implications. I&quot;m sure some people would disagree but consider this --- The spells Mutable Mask and Many Faces are duration spells that stop working when the spell ends, and then you return to your true form. I've wondered if there was a legitimate way to make these spells lasting without them being unfriendly-to-the-lore, or require archmastery, or some other obvious problems. I think I have one!<br /> <br /> Instead of the imago creating immediate changes, the changes take place over a long time as the body is slowly controlled to create these physical changes, making them lasting by virtue of them being consequences of what the spell actually does--which is to rewire your body's processes to <i>cause</i> the changes you want as a logical consequence of what the spell does. Instead of making your body more attractive in an instant and then having to maintain the spell to maintain your new looks? You cast a spell that changes how your body wants to arrange flesh, making a slow process that the mage has to follow-up on with the correct eating or exercise habits--the spell just makes it <i>easier.</i><br /> <br /> The set-back to this? You have to know what you're doing. If your imago is wrong, you could end up screwing your body up. Perhaps with a medicine or athletics + intelligence check? Unless its reasonable that knowledge of the Life Arcanum fills in those gaps already...<br /> <br /> I dunno if that's a good example since in both cases the primary factor seems sensibly to be duration. Unless your casting on someone else and then it is Withstood by stamina? Or maybe it would be Withstood by stamina even if you are targetting yourself because your body resists these sorts of changes as a matter of course? I don't know. But if so, maybe this train-of-thought helps show an example where an established spell is experimented with to get a different factor.<br /> <br /> The established spell causes effects and maintains them until the spell ends. In this creative-thaumaturgy version, the effects will last after the spell is over, but only if the spell lasted long enough to cause those effects, and the effects take time, and are at risk of dissonance in the mean-time. How's that sound?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I can't believe how wordy I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 11-13-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T03:35:14-08:00","id":1158404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1158289#post1158289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the arcana were written by different authors, so consistency would suffer just from that although I'm sure they tried to keep it as consistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I generally recommend rooting out the inconsistencies (such as Augment Mind / Honing the Form) and houseruling them to the same Primary Factor at the start of every Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-14-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T04:02:38-08:00","id":1158410,"title":"","content":"Generally, three seconds of super-intelligence is all you need. Unless it's activated reflexively, three seconds of super-strength is less useful. <br /> <br /> The power of a spell is a product of its function, not its form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T04:10:37-08:00","id":1158411,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d disagree, I can think of plenty of situations where physical abilities aren\u2019t used in anything except short bursts unless you\u2019re engaged or anticipate being engaged in an activity that will require some endurance. Need to jump? Short burst. Need to lift something heavy? Short burst","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T04:37:24-08:00","id":1158413,"title":"","content":"See, lifting something heavy I could see maybe taking maybe ten seconds or so. <br /> <br /> In other words, exactly what Honing the form gives you with no reach or extra spell factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T04:41:29-08:00","id":1158416,"title":"","content":"Also there are really not that many instances were super intelligence for three seconds is that helpful. You usually don't look at a puzzle and just solve it in three seconds of genius, while you didn't really think about it at all in the time before and after. I would also rule that Augment Mind should be duration Primary.<br /> For determining Primary Factor I also find it helping to ignore the Advanced Duration template. Since going to Advanced Potency is not actually improving Potency I often find myself thinking: &quot;Oh Potency Primary is so much better, I can just go to Advanced Duration with a reach and don't need any more than that.&quot; But if you compare them both without going to advanced I find +1 Strength/Intelligence for 3 turns usually better, than +3 Strength/Intelligence for 1 turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T04:46:43-08:00","id":1158417,"title":"","content":"If I were going to worry about putting all the buff Perfecting spells on the same Primary factor I\u2019d make them Potency primary. The boost is large and it\u2019s just a Reach to get the effects to last for a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T11:55:51-08:00","id":1158577,"title":"","content":"I would say it makes more sense for Augment Mind to be Duration, rather than Hone the Form being Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:11:15-08:00","id":1158631,"title":"","content":"In my game they are all going to be Potency as I feel that makes the most sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T06:21:37-08:00","id":1160496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057140-reach-to-switch-primary-factor?p=1158410#post1158410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, three seconds of super-intelligence is all you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to strongly disagree based on my own play experience. <br /> <br /> Most physical actions (strength-based) are instant. Mental actions in our chronicle lend more towards extended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T13:42:52-08:00","id":1160637,"title":"","content":"I think the problem isn't instant vs. extended as much as things like combat and chases where there isn't a break to cast a buff spell between actions, and social maneuvering and investigations where there is generally time to buff between intervals of action (also, I see a lot of instant Wits rolls due to perception).<br /> <br /> The game generally treats detailed physical scenes as being very immediate. A small buff to Strength for the duration of a fight with one casting is generally (obviously not always) better than one round of high Strength per casting. The action economy of combat doesn't favor cutting out half your actions towards casting spells that increase your mundane combat skills over just attacking/defending actively each round.<br /> <br /> The game generally treats social and mental scenes as having more narrative leeway. You don't need to keep your mental buff during a whole investigation, you just need them buffed in short bursts when rolling to collect a clue. When you're using Soft Leverage to open Doors, you don't need to keep buffed the whole time, just long enough to complete whatever action is supposed to appeal to the target before you go back to whatever you were doing between intervals.<br /> <br /> Generic extended actions aren't very illustrative to which is more useful in general, because they can model either scenario. A generic physical extended action could be immediate (climbing a tall tree) or something that can be done in spurts (carving a statue), as can a generic mental extended action.<br /> <br /> I don't think house ruling these to have the same primary is inherently going to be a problem (Attribute buffs are, generally speaking, going to be things you want to increase in Potency and Duration when the chips are down so in their most useful applications is when you want to increase both and which the base is matters the least), but them not being the same has mechanical logic to it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}